WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:01:09.111 --> 00:01:10.737
Turn to the right, milady.


00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:12.155
Thank you.


00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:19.037
That's it.


00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:51.195
Hear ye, hear ye, hear ye!


00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:56.158
Lords! Knights! Squires!


00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:59.161
And all other manner of people.


00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:03.540
That by the command of Our Lord,
the king of France...


00:02:03.749 --> 00:02:06.752
it is strictly prohibited...


00:02:07.503 --> 00:02:11.298
on pain of death
and the loss of property...


00:02:11.465 --> 00:02:14.009
for anyone here to be armed...


00:02:14.301 --> 00:02:16.553
or to carry a sword or dagger...


00:02:16.762 --> 00:02:20.682
unless he be one
who has the express permission...


00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:23.310
of Our Lord, the king.


00:02:25.187 --> 00:02:27.439
Each man is to fight...


00:02:27.731 --> 00:02:30.359
on horseback and on foot...


00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:31.985
armed in the manner that pleases him...


00:02:32.236 --> 00:02:35.239
with any weapon or device
of attack or defense.


00:02:35.531 --> 00:02:40.327
Except for weapons or devices
of equal design...


00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.997
or made with charms or spells...


00:02:44.206 --> 00:02:47.793
or any other thing that is
forbidden by God and holy church...


00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.837
to all good Christians.


00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:54.174
If either combatant should carry
onto the field of battle...


00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:57.761
any arms that have been
forged with spells...


00:02:58.053 --> 00:03:01.473
charms, enchantments,
or any other evil arts...


00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:05.811
then so shall the malefactor be punished
as an enemy of God...


00:03:06.979 --> 00:03:08.397
or as a traitor...


00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.733
or as a murderer.


00:03:13.986 --> 00:03:15.571
Tighter. Tighter.


00:04:11.418 --> 00:04:14.171
Knights, proceed.


00:04:42.658 --> 00:04:44.409
Let them go!


00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:48.205
Let them go! Let them go!


00:05:14.523 --> 00:05:16.650
Come for your fight!


00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:19.444
You're all gonna die!


00:05:20.779 --> 00:05:23.657
You're all gonna die like pigs!


00:05:25.492 --> 00:05:26.952
Come on, then!


00:05:27.786 --> 00:05:30.455
Come on, you failed scum...


00:05:30.622 --> 00:05:31.707
We cannot just sit here.


00:05:31.874 --> 00:05:32.708
...and fight!


00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:35.085
Jean, we were ordered by Pierre
to hold this bridge.


00:05:35.294 --> 00:05:37.254
Orders be damned.
For the king.


00:05:38.964 --> 00:05:40.632
For the king!


00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:42.551
For the king!


00:06:23.759 --> 00:06:24.760
Thank you.


00:06:31.433 --> 00:06:35.312
I will make no apology
for how you men fought today.


00:06:36.438 --> 00:06:38.524
It was an honor to be there with you.


00:06:40.108 --> 00:06:41.693
Limoges is lost.


00:06:42.736 --> 00:06:45.531
And our allies have failed
to take the port at Brest.


00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.867
Our new Lord, Pierre...


00:06:49.076 --> 00:06:52.663
has now resigned the campaign
and orders us home.


00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.790
We move at dawn.


00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.792
Hear, hear.


00:06:56.959 --> 00:06:57.960
To the king.


00:07:00.671 --> 00:07:03.131
Evidently, Pierre is not happy.


00:07:05.759 --> 00:07:06.844
Lives were saved.


00:07:07.052 --> 00:07:08.846
Not in Limoges.


00:07:09.346 --> 00:07:11.598
Let us return home, my friend.


00:07:12.766 --> 00:07:14.476
You saved my life today.


00:07:16.645 --> 00:07:17.980
Thank you.


00:07:53.599 --> 00:07:55.184
Declare yourself!


00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:57.895
Squire Jean de Carrouges.


00:07:58.103 --> 00:08:00.022
Son of the captain of this fort.


00:08:00.272 --> 00:08:01.857
Open the gates!


00:08:18.707 --> 00:08:20.375
It's a great honor
for Pierre to have chosen


00:08:20.459 --> 00:08:22.294
your father's castle for this ceremony.


00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:26.548
I shall be prepared to assume
this captaincy upon my father's passing.


00:08:26.715 --> 00:08:28.133
Pray it is not for many years.


00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.219
Father.
Mother.


00:08:30.469 --> 00:08:32.304
Captain.
Milady.


00:08:32.513 --> 00:08:34.014
Squires.


00:08:34.431 --> 00:08:36.058
Do not keep Our Lord Pierre waiting.


00:08:36.265 --> 00:08:37.808
...become your man.
I shall serve you for life.


00:08:41.563 --> 00:08:44.816
So, Lord, I become your man.
I swear I shall serve you for life.


00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:49.530
Milord, I become your man.
I shall serve you for life.


00:08:50.697 --> 00:08:53.450
Milord, I become your man.
I swear I shall serve you for life.


00:08:59.665 --> 00:09:02.543
Lord, I become your man.
I swear I shall serve you for life.


00:09:10.217 --> 00:09:11.051
-Lord...
-Closer.


00:09:14.137 --> 00:09:16.014
Lord, I become your man.


00:09:16.181 --> 00:09:18.141
I swear I shall serve you for life.


00:09:33.156 --> 00:09:34.449
Declare yourself.


00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:37.744
It is I. Helen of Troy.


00:09:40.914 --> 00:09:42.374
Le Gris.


00:09:43.667 --> 00:09:45.544
It's good to see you, my friend.


00:09:47.087 --> 00:09:49.381
Though I do not come only as a friend.


00:09:51.175 --> 00:09:54.136
I'm afraid there's more to my visit
than I have let on.


00:09:58.182 --> 00:09:59.474
Speak.


00:10:02.394 --> 00:10:05.063
Pierre has charged me
with the collection of debts.


00:10:05.397 --> 00:10:06.690
I see.


00:10:07.316 --> 00:10:10.819
I have already visited
all the other tenants in his domain.


00:10:12.571 --> 00:10:13.655
And now...


00:10:14.031 --> 00:10:15.032
You have come to see me.


00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:17.242
I have come to see you.


00:10:21.705 --> 00:10:24.499
These levies are for military defense.


00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.544
And you know as well as anyone
our enemy's present.


00:10:27.711 --> 00:10:28.712
And we need to be ready.


00:10:28.921 --> 00:10:31.215
When have I not been ready to stand
and fight for my king?


00:10:31.381 --> 00:10:32.216
You have.


00:10:32.424 --> 00:10:34.343
More than any other.


00:10:35.052 --> 00:10:36.512
But that's not all this Pierre wants.


00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:37.679
No, what Pierre wants...


00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.848
Pierre wants the money
that he's rightfully owed.


00:10:46.021 --> 00:10:47.481
I don't have it.


00:10:48.273 --> 00:10:50.275
This plague has carried off
half my workforce.


00:10:50.442 --> 00:10:51.818
My rent collection is down.


00:10:51.985 --> 00:10:53.362
My fields yield half what they used to.


00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:55.781
And the cost of labor has now risen.


00:10:56.406 --> 00:10:57.616
Yes.


00:11:00.869 --> 00:11:02.538
How is it the other vassals paid?


00:11:03.372 --> 00:11:05.582
They paid because I had to insist.


00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:07.751
I see.


00:11:07.918 --> 00:11:10.045
And now, you insist upon me?


00:11:14.591 --> 00:11:15.467
Let me talk to Pierre.


00:11:17.886 --> 00:11:19.972
He's not without reason.


00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.890
I will explain your situation.


00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.852
You are a true friend.


00:11:25.018 --> 00:11:27.312
But I cannot return empty-handed.


00:11:27.479 --> 00:11:28.856
Of course not.


00:11:31.483 --> 00:11:32.860
Thank you.


00:11:34.486 --> 00:11:36.029
Let me see what I have at hand.


00:11:57.968 --> 00:11:59.511
-Think about this.
-I have.


00:11:59.678 --> 00:12:00.512
You have not.


00:12:00.721 --> 00:12:02.306
I will be fighting
under Admiral de Vienne.


00:12:02.514 --> 00:12:04.933
The English are looting
the Cotentin Peninsula as we speak.


00:12:05.142 --> 00:12:06.643
This plague has taken your wife and son.


00:12:06.894 --> 00:12:07.936
I will not stand by
whilst Lower Normandy falls.


00:12:08.103 --> 00:12:09.396
Do not let this obduracy take you.


00:12:09.563 --> 00:12:10.606
You have no heir.


00:12:10.939 --> 00:12:13.150
If you die, all you have
will revert to Count Pierre.


00:12:14.443 --> 00:12:16.236
A fact not lost on Pierre, I'm certain.


00:12:16.445 --> 00:12:17.863
He does not favor me as he does you.


00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:19.198
No, you have much to live for.


00:12:19.364 --> 00:12:21.074
What do I have to live for, here? What?


00:12:21.283 --> 00:12:22.576
A name.


00:12:22.784 --> 00:12:26.413
It's too great and storied a name
for you to treat it so recklessly.


00:12:26.872 --> 00:12:28.999
Your father has the captaincy of Bellême.


00:12:29.249 --> 00:12:31.001
When he dies,
you will inherit that garrison


00:12:31.084 --> 00:12:32.252
and everything that comes with it.


00:12:32.461 --> 00:12:34.004
And I am your friend.


00:12:34.963 --> 00:12:38.383
And there are many others like me
who would prefer you not perish.


00:12:39.927 --> 00:12:42.763
I don't embark
on this campaign recklessly.


00:12:43.639 --> 00:12:45.349
I don't embark on it just to fight.


00:12:45.891 --> 00:12:47.226
Then why?


00:12:48.435 --> 00:12:49.770
Jacques.


00:12:52.356 --> 00:12:53.565
I am...


00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:56.109
broke.


00:12:57.819 --> 00:12:59.154
I need money.


00:13:52.332 --> 00:13:55.002
Long live the king!


00:13:56.545 --> 00:13:58.380
Long live the king!


00:14:16.481 --> 00:14:18.483
-They're back!
-Quick! Come on! They're back!


00:14:31.788 --> 00:14:34.374
-I'll take that from you.
-Let me help you, sir.


00:14:34.791 --> 00:14:36.627
Turn around, please, my lord.


00:14:39.755 --> 00:14:41.590
Lift, lift your arm.


00:14:43.717 --> 00:14:44.968
Take them more bread.


00:14:45.385 --> 00:14:46.803
Over here. They want some more.


00:15:05.989 --> 00:15:07.950
Robert de Thibouville.


00:15:08.116 --> 00:15:10.953
He's providing shelter and vittles for us.


00:15:12.162 --> 00:15:13.539
De Thibouville?


00:15:14.748 --> 00:15:17.209
Did he not side with the English
against us at Poitiers?


00:15:17.543 --> 00:15:19.920
Yes, but he was pardoned
along with the others.


00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:21.755
He's with us now.


00:15:21.964 --> 00:15:24.258
And he'll stay that way
if he knows what's good for him.


00:15:24.466 --> 00:15:25.592
Steady, Jean.


00:15:25.843 --> 00:15:27.469
It's a roof over our heads.


00:15:27.761 --> 00:15:29.179
Besides...


00:15:29.555 --> 00:15:31.849
he has quite the wine cellar.


00:15:47.823 --> 00:15:49.116
What a beauty.


00:15:50.993 --> 00:15:52.286
She is a de Thibouville?


00:15:52.536 --> 00:15:54.830
Yes. Her name is even older than yours.


00:15:55.205 --> 00:15:56.999
She's his only daughter.


00:15:57.249 --> 00:15:59.293
There's a dowry to be had.


00:15:59.459 --> 00:16:02.129
Of course, a man would have to bear
the mark of her father's disgrace...


00:16:02.296 --> 00:16:05.257
I don't imagine
one would suffer too greatly


00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:07.050
at the task of producing an heir.


00:16:09.428 --> 00:16:11.013
Gentlemen, welcome.


00:16:11.555 --> 00:16:13.182
You fought bravely.


00:16:14.349 --> 00:16:15.559
Thank you for hosting us.


00:16:15.767 --> 00:16:18.061
-I would like to introduce...
-Jean de Carrouges.


00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:20.397
Your reputation precedes you.


00:16:20.606 --> 00:16:22.399
As does yours.


00:16:23.942 --> 00:16:26.069
It's my pleasure to host you and your men.


00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:29.281
It is only just to support the men
who fight for the king.


00:16:31.116 --> 00:16:33.535
Some lessons
are learned later in life, hmm?


00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.457
Allow me to introduce my daughter.


00:16:38.707 --> 00:16:39.875
Marguerite.


00:16:40.209 --> 00:16:43.086
Marguerite,
this is Squire Jean de Carrouges.


00:16:44.338 --> 00:16:46.965
Milady, I'm pleased to meet you.


00:16:48.091 --> 00:16:49.676
Pleasure is mine.


00:17:00.562 --> 00:17:03.357
The dowry includes this parcel as well.


00:17:03.857 --> 00:17:06.443
Starting at the hunting grounds.


00:17:12.031 --> 00:17:14.326
What of this here? The one to the north?


00:17:15.202 --> 00:17:16.954
Aunou-le-Faucon.


00:17:21.083 --> 00:17:24.294
As I say, starting at the hunting grounds.


00:17:35.472 --> 00:17:37.516
I'll have that piece of land as well.


00:17:38.475 --> 00:17:40.435
Most certainly.


00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.786
Amen.


00:18:39.286 --> 00:18:41.788
I'm a very jealous man, milady.


00:18:41.955 --> 00:18:45.042
Tonight, you are mine
and will dance with no other.


00:18:46.543 --> 00:18:48.754
And every night hereafter.


00:19:24.706 --> 00:19:26.375
No need to worry.


00:19:31.421 --> 00:19:32.923
This is it.


00:19:39.263 --> 00:19:40.764
Property starts at the river mouth...


00:19:41.014 --> 00:19:44.017
and extends
all the way to the hill beyond.


00:19:44.226 --> 00:19:46.061
So, this is Aunou-le-Faucon.


00:19:47.187 --> 00:19:50.065
This was meant to be
part of Marguerite's dowry.


00:19:50.232 --> 00:19:51.775
She loved it here.


00:19:52.192 --> 00:19:54.194
And Pierre simply gave it to you.


00:19:54.403 --> 00:19:56.780
In appreciation of my service.


00:19:58.615 --> 00:20:00.826
His accounts were in complete chaos.


00:20:01.034 --> 00:20:03.871
Once I was able to reorder them
and collect the rents due...


00:20:04.037 --> 00:20:06.957
everything started functioning properly,
and his fortunes turned.


00:20:07.165 --> 00:20:10.377
Gave me this as a sign of his gratitude.


00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:16.383
It's not my doing.


00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:19.261
The count is generous and impetuous.


00:20:24.725 --> 00:20:26.351
Let us eat.


00:20:34.902 --> 00:20:37.571
I wish you'd seen the gardens
at Aunou-le-Faucon.


00:20:37.863 --> 00:20:40.199
We had roses and lavender.


00:20:40.657 --> 00:20:42.576
Then, we shall have those here.


00:20:42.826 --> 00:20:46.455
I remember my father built a swing
on the largest tree in the estate.


00:20:46.663 --> 00:20:49.917
I will find the largest tree
and do the same.


00:20:50.959 --> 00:20:53.879
I have such wonderful memories
of my summers there.


00:20:57.132 --> 00:21:01.178
It's a pity Pierre took that estate
from your father.


00:21:01.553 --> 00:21:02.554
I know you miss it.


00:21:03.639 --> 00:21:06.475
It's the only way
he could pay what he owed.


00:21:07.768 --> 00:21:11.480
Pierre then just gave it
to Jacques Le Gris as a gift.


00:21:12.481 --> 00:21:15.108
Do all squires enjoy such lavish gifts?


00:21:15.859 --> 00:21:17.611
Le Gris more than most.


00:21:18.487 --> 00:21:21.323
He has become Pierre's most trusted.


00:21:23.158 --> 00:21:26.078
Perhaps Aunou-le-Faucon
is not gone for good.


00:21:28.247 --> 00:21:30.457
Perhaps I shall not let that rest.


00:21:32.125 --> 00:21:33.252
Jean.


00:21:34.002 --> 00:21:36.171
My love, I have bled for this king.


00:21:36.922 --> 00:21:38.173
He knows of me.


00:21:39.424 --> 00:21:41.385
I may have more power than you think.


00:21:42.052 --> 00:21:44.388
I know how powerful you are.


00:21:47.975 --> 00:21:51.603
This land was promised to me
as part of my wife's dowry.


00:21:52.729 --> 00:21:54.731
The petition is denied.


00:21:55.816 --> 00:21:59.653
This decision comes directly
from His Majesty, the king.


00:22:12.207 --> 00:22:14.209
Are you Squire Jean de Carrouges?


00:22:14.459 --> 00:22:15.752
That is I.


00:22:17.796 --> 00:22:18.839
What does it say?


00:22:19.047 --> 00:22:20.591
'Tis your father.


00:22:35.981 --> 00:22:37.149
Open the gate!


00:22:37.482 --> 00:22:38.650
Open the gate!


00:22:41.987 --> 00:22:43.280
Leave us.


00:22:51.455 --> 00:22:53.749
I was in Paris when the news came.


00:22:56.376 --> 00:22:58.378
Your father died quietly.


00:22:58.545 --> 00:23:00.088
In his sleep.


00:23:02.674 --> 00:23:04.051
I am lost.


00:23:05.719 --> 00:23:08.138
They tell me I'm to leave here
within a month.


00:23:10.849 --> 00:23:13.060
You will do no such thing.


00:23:13.227 --> 00:23:15.062
I will assume the captaincy.


00:23:15.229 --> 00:23:16.939
You will keep
your quarters, your servants.


00:23:17.022 --> 00:23:17.856
Everything will be the way it was...


00:23:18.023 --> 00:23:19.775
Jean, have you not heard?


00:23:19.983 --> 00:23:22.110
You're not going to follow
in your father's footsteps...


00:23:22.319 --> 00:23:24.780
as captain here at Bellême.


00:23:24.947 --> 00:23:26.448
What do you mean?


00:23:27.115 --> 00:23:31.119
Why did you have to sue the count
for a piece of land?


00:23:31.286 --> 00:23:33.080
Just to impress your bride.


00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:35.999
That land was promised to me.
It was an appeal.


00:23:36.208 --> 00:23:38.043
And now, you've made an enemy
of Count Pierre.


00:23:38.293 --> 00:23:39.670
It was right.


00:23:40.546 --> 00:23:43.298
Right. There's no right.


00:23:43.465 --> 00:23:45.926
There is only the power of men.


00:23:48.262 --> 00:23:51.598
You sued him,
and you've made a powerful enemy.


00:23:53.934 --> 00:23:55.435
Your father was a hard man


00:23:55.519 --> 00:23:58.772
but there was much about this world
that he understood.


00:24:03.193 --> 00:24:08.240
Who then will assume
my father's captaincy?


00:24:41.023 --> 00:24:42.274
Good day!


00:24:43.984 --> 00:24:45.819
Join us, my squire.


00:24:46.069 --> 00:24:47.613
This is a day for celebration.


00:24:50.741 --> 00:24:52.576
I will not be staying, milord.


00:24:53.493 --> 00:24:56.288
I do not wish to interrupt
such an occasion...


00:24:57.706 --> 00:25:00.209
but my honor compels me to speak.


00:25:03.795 --> 00:25:06.798
I was angered, but I spoke well.


00:25:06.965 --> 00:25:08.467
I said to Pierre...


00:25:08.759 --> 00:25:11.970
"Can you stand there, as a man of honor,
as my liege lord...


00:25:12.221 --> 00:25:15.015
"and say that I am not man enough
to assume my rightful captaincy...


00:25:15.224 --> 00:25:18.852
"that my grandfather and my father
held for the last 20 years of his life...


00:25:19.436 --> 00:25:23.357
"and take command of that garrison
and hold the fort of Bellême for my king?"


00:25:23.565 --> 00:25:24.566
And what said Pierre?


00:25:24.775 --> 00:25:26.276
And there was Le Gris...


00:25:26.693 --> 00:25:29.905
whose life I saved, sitting by his side...


00:25:30.072 --> 00:25:33.075
with his captaincy,
not even man enough to look at me.


00:25:34.243 --> 00:25:36.453
He poisons milord with evil advice.


00:25:36.703 --> 00:25:38.830
Whispered in his ear, blackening my name.


00:25:41.416 --> 00:25:43.377
Surely, you did not say this.


00:25:45.587 --> 00:25:47.548
You did.


00:25:52.469 --> 00:25:54.263
We are no longer welcome at court.


00:25:55.097 --> 00:25:56.098
Jean...


00:25:56.306 --> 00:25:57.391
So be it.


00:26:15.909 --> 00:26:17.119
Milord.


00:26:17.703 --> 00:26:19.621
Jean, an invitation has arrived.


00:26:22.124 --> 00:26:24.668
Your friend Jean Crespin
has invited us to his home.


00:26:24.918 --> 00:26:27.379
They are celebrating
the birth of their first child.


00:26:28.297 --> 00:26:30.215
It's a boy.


00:26:30.382 --> 00:26:31.967
Wonderful news.


00:26:32.384 --> 00:26:34.052
It's been a year since Bellême.


00:26:35.721 --> 00:26:37.264
Perhaps we may show our faces...


00:26:37.431 --> 00:26:40.017
so they know we carry on
in spite of this injustice.


00:26:41.351 --> 00:26:43.478
A healthy child in these times...


00:26:43.729 --> 00:26:45.898
is cause for a celebration.


00:26:47.983 --> 00:26:52.154
Do you think I would deny
the rabble of Argentan...


00:26:52.404 --> 00:26:54.865
the sight of a true noblewoman?


00:26:56.366 --> 00:26:58.160
Have a gown made.


00:27:09.171 --> 00:27:12.007
This one is ready.
We need more hay over here.


00:27:42.120 --> 00:27:44.081
I am very glad you chose to attend.


00:27:44.248 --> 00:27:46.208
This will only do you good, my love.


00:27:47.251 --> 00:27:49.711
Jean, I'm very pleased to see you.
It's been a long time.


00:27:49.878 --> 00:27:51.463
Congratulations, my friend.


00:27:51.797 --> 00:27:53.298
-Milady, you look lovely.
-Thank you.


00:27:53.465 --> 00:27:55.342
Please, you're most welcome.


00:28:13.777 --> 00:28:15.237
Pardon me, milady.


00:28:27.332 --> 00:28:29.084
-Le Gris.
-Carrouges.


00:28:29.793 --> 00:28:33.046
Pax! Well done! Well done, all!


00:28:33.255 --> 00:28:35.549
Let there be no ill will
among the servants of the king.


00:28:35.757 --> 00:28:36.758
He needs us all right now.


00:28:36.925 --> 00:28:39.511
Hear, hear. Well spoken, old friend.


00:28:39.678 --> 00:28:40.721
Marguerite, come.


00:28:40.929 --> 00:28:44.766
Give our old friend a kiss and show
the good faith of the house Carrouges.


00:29:06.914 --> 00:29:08.999
I will return
in just a few months, my love.


00:29:09.208 --> 00:29:11.502
I will be safe and well attended to
by Alice and your mother...


00:29:11.668 --> 00:29:12.836
but I will miss you.


00:29:13.045 --> 00:29:14.129
This is what I do.


00:29:15.047 --> 00:29:16.131
Let me provide for you.


00:29:16.298 --> 00:29:18.091
And what of you?


00:29:18.342 --> 00:29:19.927
I have all that I need.


00:29:20.385 --> 00:29:22.012
Except an heir.


00:29:22.638 --> 00:29:23.639
My love.


00:29:25.933 --> 00:29:27.559
It comes as God wills it.


00:29:54.336 --> 00:29:57.130
Be thou a knight in the name of God.


00:29:58.131 --> 00:29:59.258
Rise.


00:30:01.385 --> 00:30:03.095
Jean de Carrouges!


00:30:05.222 --> 00:30:07.266
In honor of your service to our king.


00:30:11.311 --> 00:30:12.354
Quiet!


00:30:17.067 --> 00:30:19.403
Be thou a knight in the name of God.


00:30:20.028 --> 00:30:21.154
Rise.


00:30:29.121 --> 00:30:33.083
All right, men!
Make preparations for battle!


00:30:50.434 --> 00:30:51.560
Sire?


00:31:12.039 --> 00:31:13.332
Why do they run?


00:31:14.374 --> 00:31:15.334
Why do they run?


00:31:18.795 --> 00:31:20.005
For the king!


00:31:33.519 --> 00:31:35.103
Our lord returns!


00:31:35.479 --> 00:31:36.897
They're coming!


00:31:37.356 --> 00:31:39.149
Our lord returns!


00:31:40.442 --> 00:31:42.069
Our lord returns!


00:31:47.574 --> 00:31:49.117
Our lord returns!


00:31:49.284 --> 00:31:50.827
He's coming!


00:32:03.215 --> 00:32:04.591
Welcome back, sire!


00:32:37.499 --> 00:32:39.501
Milord, you are not well.


00:32:40.961 --> 00:32:44.089
This fever is all I've brought back
from that wretched place.


00:32:45.215 --> 00:32:47.050
As well as your knighthood.


00:32:48.385 --> 00:32:50.095
Tomorrow, I must go to Paris.


00:32:51.471 --> 00:32:52.347
I'll be away one week.


00:32:52.514 --> 00:32:53.473
What do you want?


00:32:53.640 --> 00:32:55.058
I'm owed money by the treasurer.


00:32:55.225 --> 00:32:56.518
Jean, you are unwell.


00:32:56.727 --> 00:32:58.312
He's well enough to travel.


00:32:59.563 --> 00:33:00.689
To Paris?


00:33:00.898 --> 00:33:02.274
That's three days' ride.


00:33:02.441 --> 00:33:03.775
And Argentan.


00:33:04.276 --> 00:33:06.862
Duty demands that I report to Pierre.


00:33:08.405 --> 00:33:10.240
They will admire you as a knight.


00:33:11.241 --> 00:33:14.828
And you will confound those who had
not expected you to return, Sir Jean.


00:34:28.610 --> 00:34:30.445
Sir Jean de Carrouges?


00:34:36.827 --> 00:34:38.495
Signature here.


00:34:48.589 --> 00:34:50.132
300 gold pieces.


00:35:12.905 --> 00:35:14.198
Sire.


00:35:45.854 --> 00:35:47.689
I will be in my chamber.


00:35:48.690 --> 00:35:50.025
Good night.


00:35:56.281 --> 00:35:57.491
My love?


00:36:00.369 --> 00:36:02.496
What is the matter?


00:36:02.663 --> 00:36:04.748
Has my mother
quarreled with you yet again?


00:36:07.167 --> 00:36:08.168
No.


00:36:15.467 --> 00:36:16.510
I have missed you.


00:36:21.348 --> 00:36:23.058
Did you not miss me?


00:36:24.601 --> 00:36:25.936
I missed you more than you know.


00:36:26.103 --> 00:36:28.021
Then let us go to bed.


00:36:28.188 --> 00:36:29.982
What? What is it, my love?


00:36:43.412 --> 00:36:46.248
When you were gone, there was a day...


00:36:47.165 --> 00:36:50.043
when your mother had business
in Saint Pierre.


00:36:50.252 --> 00:36:51.420
Yes.


00:36:53.881 --> 00:36:58.635
She took the servants with her
on her errand, and I was left alone.


00:36:59.386 --> 00:37:00.929
Did she not leave Alice?


00:37:01.096 --> 00:37:02.431
I told her in no uncertain terms.


00:37:02.598 --> 00:37:04.725
She took all the servants.


00:37:08.979 --> 00:37:12.107
Shortly after, a man came unannounced.


00:37:14.401 --> 00:37:16.195
I knew the man, so I let him in.


00:37:17.321 --> 00:37:18.906
But he was not alone.


00:37:23.660 --> 00:37:25.245
He attacked me.


00:37:28.373 --> 00:37:31.293
He pinned me down, I protested.


00:37:32.920 --> 00:37:36.673
I screamed, I cried out as best I could,
but there was no one here.


00:37:38.383 --> 00:37:40.886
I was overpowered.
There was nothing I could do.


00:37:49.353 --> 00:37:50.812
I was raped.


00:37:53.148 --> 00:37:55.442
Who? Who did this?


00:37:56.151 --> 00:37:57.361
Who?


00:37:58.612 --> 00:37:59.571
Jacques Le Gris.


00:38:06.745 --> 00:38:08.705
Are you telling me the truth?


00:38:09.081 --> 00:38:10.749
Yes. Yes.


00:38:10.958 --> 00:38:12.835
-Are you telling me the truth?
-Yes, I am telling you the truth.


00:38:13.001 --> 00:38:14.628
You must believe me.


00:38:16.547 --> 00:38:17.422
You must.


00:38:19.675 --> 00:38:21.301
You are my beloved.


00:38:21.468 --> 00:38:22.511
Here.


00:38:25.472 --> 00:38:27.307
I was not here to protect you.


00:38:30.394 --> 00:38:31.979
Please forgive me.


00:38:34.147 --> 00:38:35.232
Please.


00:38:35.858 --> 00:38:37.150
Jean.


00:38:38.485 --> 00:38:41.363
I want him to answer for what he has done.


00:38:42.197 --> 00:38:43.490
And he will.


00:38:46.577 --> 00:38:47.786
He will.


00:38:56.044 --> 00:38:56.962
Collect the swords!


00:38:57.671 --> 00:38:59.006
Show them in, please.


00:39:00.090 --> 00:39:01.175
Take the horses down.


00:39:02.551 --> 00:39:03.802
Move them aside.


00:39:05.304 --> 00:39:06.388
Show them in, please.


00:39:06.555 --> 00:39:08.348
And so, I ask for your help.


00:39:08.891 --> 00:39:12.227
Marguerite is my wife,
and she has been wronged.


00:39:14.146 --> 00:39:15.939
I will not allow this to go unpunished.


00:39:16.106 --> 00:39:18.442
Your only avenue is through Pierre.


00:39:19.026 --> 00:39:20.903
Though I doubt he will give you a hearing.


00:39:23.530 --> 00:39:25.574
Tell the story you've heard today.


00:39:25.866 --> 00:39:28.535
Tell it anywhere you can
and to all who will listen.


00:39:28.702 --> 00:39:30.746
We will be the subject of gossip.


00:39:30.954 --> 00:39:33.498
If the story is known across Normandy...


00:39:34.291 --> 00:39:36.293
Pierre will have to grant us a hearing.


00:39:38.629 --> 00:39:40.005
I have a plan.


00:39:47.387 --> 00:39:49.014
I request a duel to the death.


00:39:49.932 --> 00:39:52.684
This custom was outlawed years ago.


00:39:53.352 --> 00:39:55.187
Not so, Your Grace.


00:39:55.354 --> 00:39:58.982
It is true that no duels have been fought
during your lifetime...


00:39:59.233 --> 00:40:01.735
though it remains acceptable as a venue...


00:40:01.944 --> 00:40:05.697
It would require a full convening of
the assembled parliamentary body of Paris.


00:40:05.864 --> 00:40:08.617
All 32 members of Your Majesty's court.


00:40:09.326 --> 00:40:10.786
One of us has lied.


00:40:11.870 --> 00:40:13.163
Let us let God decide.


00:40:13.372 --> 00:40:16.500
Sir Jean, if you lose this duel...


00:40:16.667 --> 00:40:19.419
thus proving these accusations false...


00:40:19.962 --> 00:40:22.297
your wife would suffer dire consequences.


00:40:23.799 --> 00:40:26.134
God will spare those who tell the truth.


00:40:26.635 --> 00:40:28.428
And the truth will prevail.


00:40:29.388 --> 00:40:30.889
I am not afraid.


00:40:32.140 --> 00:40:33.308
Excellent.


00:41:02.504 --> 00:41:06.550
His Majesty, King Charles VI!


00:41:07.467 --> 00:41:10.804
What is your business today
before this court?


00:41:24.776 --> 00:41:26.820
Most excellent and powerful king...


00:41:26.987 --> 00:41:28.155
and our sovereign lord...


00:41:29.531 --> 00:41:31.450
I present myself...


00:41:31.617 --> 00:41:33.327
Jean de Carrouges...


00:41:33.493 --> 00:41:34.786
knight...


00:41:36.163 --> 00:41:38.290
as an appellant in your court...


00:41:39.666 --> 00:41:43.754
and hereby do accuse this squire...


00:41:43.921 --> 00:41:46.215
of a most foul crime...


00:41:46.381 --> 00:41:47.799
against my wife...


00:41:48.509 --> 00:41:50.594
the Lady Marguerite de Carrouges.


00:41:51.553 --> 00:41:54.973
I charge that during the third week
of this January past...


00:41:55.140 --> 00:41:57.059
this same Jacques Le Gris...


00:41:58.477 --> 00:42:00.187
did feloniously...


00:42:00.646 --> 00:42:01.855
and carnally...


00:42:02.022 --> 00:42:06.026
take my wife against her will
in our house.


00:42:07.653 --> 00:42:11.323
And if this said Jacques Le Gris...


00:42:11.573 --> 00:42:14.243
denies his crime...


00:42:15.160 --> 00:42:16.787
I stand ready...


00:42:17.329 --> 00:42:20.958
to prove my charge
by my body against his...


00:42:21.124 --> 00:42:24.878
and to render him dead
at an appointed time.


00:42:42.813 --> 00:42:45.148
Come for your fight!


00:42:45.649 --> 00:42:47.860
You're all gonna die!


00:42:48.861 --> 00:42:51.446
You're all gonna die like pigs!


00:42:53.490 --> 00:42:55.075
Come on, then!


00:42:55.617 --> 00:42:58.036
Come on, you failed scum...


00:42:58.245 --> 00:42:59.246
We cannot just sit here.


00:42:59.454 --> 00:43:00.581
...and fight!


00:43:00.789 --> 00:43:03.166
Jean, we were ordered by Pierre
to hold this bridge.


00:43:03.417 --> 00:43:05.335
-Orders be damned.
-They're baiting you, Jean.


00:43:05.544 --> 00:43:07.713
They want us to leave the bridge
so they can take Limoges.


00:43:10.674 --> 00:43:12.676
Then they shall have their wish!


00:43:14.219 --> 00:43:15.596
My son is a fool. Let him go!


00:43:15.762 --> 00:43:17.097
If he goes alone, he will die.


00:43:17.264 --> 00:43:18.515
For the king!


00:43:18.974 --> 00:43:20.184
For the king!


00:43:49.838 --> 00:43:50.923
I know he is stubborn.


00:43:51.089 --> 00:43:52.883
Yes, stubborn, difficult, jealous...


00:43:53.091 --> 00:43:55.886
-rash, dimwitted, irascible, dimwitted...
-Yes. Yes, yes, I know, milord.


00:43:56.053 --> 00:43:58.096
...stupid. He does not exactly
yield his rents on time.


00:43:58.263 --> 00:43:59.681
But I count him as a friend.


00:44:01.099 --> 00:44:03.769
He disobeyed me and let Limoges fall.


00:44:03.977 --> 00:44:07.356
He believed he would succeed.
His intentions were good.


00:44:07.523 --> 00:44:09.942
He's no fucking fun.


00:44:10.526 --> 00:44:13.987
You mean, you'd like to see
more of his gloom here in Argentan?


00:44:14.238 --> 00:44:16.823
He postures and mopes about
like a black cloud.


00:44:17.074 --> 00:44:20.953
Milord, I have fought with him
and seen the worst of this world with him.


00:44:21.954 --> 00:44:22.996
He is loyal.


00:44:23.413 --> 00:44:25.499
Yeah. So are my fucking hounds.


00:44:27.960 --> 00:44:30.420
As you wish. Take your leave.
Do as you like.


00:44:30.671 --> 00:44:33.090
I think very little of his character.


00:44:33.382 --> 00:44:35.300
However, I think a great deal of yours.


00:44:35.509 --> 00:44:37.678
It's the quality that most recommends you.


00:44:38.387 --> 00:44:40.514
But do not let your loyalty blind you.


00:44:42.850 --> 00:44:44.184
-Thank you, milord.
-Yes.


00:44:45.769 --> 00:44:47.271
Le Gris?


00:44:47.604 --> 00:44:50.440
The gold? Or the sandal?


00:44:51.483 --> 00:44:52.818
-Gold.
-Indeed.


00:44:52.985 --> 00:44:53.902
The gold.


00:45:06.915 --> 00:45:08.792
No, no. I know, I know...


00:45:13.338 --> 00:45:14.631
Ladies and gentlemen.


00:45:19.511 --> 00:45:20.929
Ladies and gentlemen.


00:45:21.263 --> 00:45:26.268
Under ordinary circumstances,
your hostess, the viscountess...


00:45:26.435 --> 00:45:29.271
my wife, Lady Marie Chamaillart...


00:45:30.314 --> 00:45:33.025
would see the sun come up
with all of us...


00:45:33.192 --> 00:45:35.194
sing louder, dance more...


00:45:35.402 --> 00:45:37.154
and drink you all under the table.


00:45:37.821 --> 00:45:40.824
However, she's fast at work
growing our eighth child...


00:45:41.033 --> 00:45:42.910
in 14 years of marriage.


00:45:47.372 --> 00:45:49.416
Well, good night, dear friends.


00:45:49.625 --> 00:45:51.835
I shall wait up
for absolutely none of you.


00:45:52.794 --> 00:45:54.254
Especially my husband.


00:45:55.214 --> 00:45:56.048
Good night, dear.


00:45:56.256 --> 00:45:57.341
My love.


00:45:58.008 --> 00:45:59.051
Hear, hear.


00:45:59.593 --> 00:46:00.636
Good night.


00:46:05.474 --> 00:46:09.102
Well, now, perhaps the evening
can truly begin.


00:46:11.230 --> 00:46:12.314
Where were we?


00:46:13.649 --> 00:46:14.775
Latour, read.


00:46:15.692 --> 00:46:17.778
I do not read Latin.


00:46:18.529 --> 00:46:19.821
You do not even read.


00:46:20.822 --> 00:46:22.991
I will read. The Book of Love.


00:46:24.159 --> 00:46:26.119
Rule number 24.


00:46:31.750 --> 00:46:32.835
Anyone?


00:46:35.879 --> 00:46:37.130
Squire?


00:46:41.260 --> 00:46:43.720
"A new love expels an old one."


00:46:48.016 --> 00:46:49.309
Too true.


00:46:49.476 --> 00:46:52.896
Well, it appears we have a squire
with a hidden talent.


00:46:53.146 --> 00:46:54.481
Read, do read.


00:47:03.615 --> 00:47:04.992
The rule of love number four.


00:47:05.158 --> 00:47:08.161
"Love is always growing...


00:47:08.996 --> 00:47:09.997
"or diminishing."


00:47:10.747 --> 00:47:11.790
Insolent bastard!


00:47:13.584 --> 00:47:15.085
He knows you.


00:47:23.177 --> 00:47:27.347
"Nothing prevents a woman
from being loved by two men.


00:47:33.395 --> 00:47:35.647
"Or a man from being loved by two women."


00:47:39.568 --> 00:47:40.903
Well read.


00:47:44.531 --> 00:47:45.824
Oh. Come, come.


00:47:46.033 --> 00:47:48.410
If you run, I will only chase you.


00:47:55.167 --> 00:47:57.252
Wow, he grows serious.


00:47:57.586 --> 00:47:59.505
No! No! No!


00:48:00.756 --> 00:48:01.882
No!


00:48:06.386 --> 00:48:09.473
No! No! No!


00:48:13.435 --> 00:48:15.812
No! No! No!


00:48:21.985 --> 00:48:23.362
This customer is rough.


00:48:24.196 --> 00:48:25.030
No!


00:48:25.364 --> 00:48:26.657
And strong.


00:48:28.784 --> 00:48:31.578
Here, come take some evil inside you.


00:48:34.790 --> 00:48:35.832
Pierre!


00:48:36.041 --> 00:48:37.125
Come, Pierre.


00:48:38.085 --> 00:48:38.877
Great!


00:48:39.044 --> 00:48:39.837
Pierre.


00:48:40.128 --> 00:48:40.963
Pierre.


00:48:48.136 --> 00:48:49.429
Life is good.


00:48:52.266 --> 00:48:54.226
The wolves have not slept, either.


00:48:56.228 --> 00:48:58.021
Your wife will awaken soon, milord.


00:48:58.897 --> 00:49:00.774
Best be in there when she does.


00:49:01.149 --> 00:49:02.734
Pregnant and hysterical.


00:49:02.901 --> 00:49:04.778
I prefer to take my chances
with the wolves.


00:49:06.989 --> 00:49:08.782
So, tell me, squire...


00:49:09.700 --> 00:49:12.536
how does a man of war
become so learned in letters?


00:49:12.953 --> 00:49:15.372
I was born with neither a name nor wealth.


00:49:15.581 --> 00:49:17.958
I prepared for a life in the church.


00:49:19.459 --> 00:49:21.128
The requirements...


00:49:22.462 --> 00:49:23.463
did not suit me.


00:49:23.672 --> 00:49:24.673
No, no.


00:49:25.465 --> 00:49:27.009
A libertine after my own heart.


00:49:27.217 --> 00:49:28.552
That always came to me easily.


00:49:29.803 --> 00:49:32.681
Does that knowledge also apply to numbers?


00:49:33.724 --> 00:49:34.766
It does, milord.


00:49:35.642 --> 00:49:38.353
Then let me share this with you,
and this stays between us.


00:49:38.562 --> 00:49:39.813
Of course.


00:49:39.980 --> 00:49:42.274
My accounts are in disarray.


00:49:42.900 --> 00:49:45.777
Would you mind bringing your expertise
to bear on my finances?


00:49:48.405 --> 00:49:49.531
How can this be?


00:49:50.657 --> 00:49:53.452
Rents are late to come in.
The accountants are careless.


00:49:55.162 --> 00:49:58.540
Milord, these nobles are holding the money
that they are meant to yield up to you.


00:49:59.041 --> 00:50:00.918
The plague has carried off
half our workforce.


00:50:01.084 --> 00:50:02.961
Crop yields are down. Labor costs are up.


00:50:03.128 --> 00:50:06.048
I understand the numbers, and absolutely
none of this is your concern.


00:50:06.840 --> 00:50:09.092
You need to be prepared to raise an army
at a moment's notice.


00:50:09.301 --> 00:50:11.303
None of this works if you're not solvent.


00:50:12.137 --> 00:50:14.389
And when they say they do not have it?


00:50:15.057 --> 00:50:16.725
Well, let them say that to me.


00:50:18.560 --> 00:50:19.853
Well, then.


00:50:32.115 --> 00:50:33.534
I was trying to
have a word with your lord.


00:50:33.742 --> 00:50:36.662
This matter is between us.
Do not interrupt me again.


00:50:37.037 --> 00:50:38.038
All right, let us look at the map.


00:50:39.373 --> 00:50:40.207
Shall we?


00:50:44.294 --> 00:50:46.797
There is, of course,
my property here at Bourg.


00:50:48.590 --> 00:50:50.592
No. My good man, no.


00:50:50.968 --> 00:50:53.011
What's this here?


00:50:53.178 --> 00:50:54.263
Aunou-le-Faucon.


00:50:55.305 --> 00:50:56.306
No.


00:50:57.391 --> 00:50:59.685
It's one of my most valuable estates.


00:51:05.190 --> 00:51:07.901
It is to be part of my daughter's dowry.


00:51:11.572 --> 00:51:13.991
I cannot just give it to him.


00:51:15.325 --> 00:51:19.830
My friend, Pierre's not asking you
to give him your finest estate.


00:51:20.622 --> 00:51:23.667
But Aunou-le-Faucon
is worth twice what I owe.


00:51:23.876 --> 00:51:27.087
Well, think of how good it will feel
to be completely without debt.


00:51:56.992 --> 00:51:58.869
Have you heard? Reports from the north.


00:51:59.244 --> 00:52:01.580
They say there's a father so desperate...


00:52:01.747 --> 00:52:05.042
he'll marry his own daughter
to Jean de Carrouges.


00:52:05.584 --> 00:52:06.627
Indeed?


00:52:06.877 --> 00:52:10.172
Yes, Robert de Thibouville, the traitor.


00:52:12.549 --> 00:52:14.092
Carrouges needs an heir.


00:52:14.510 --> 00:52:16.595
Is she the only noblewoman in Normandy?


00:52:16.803 --> 00:52:18.180
He needs money as well.


00:52:18.430 --> 00:52:20.140
There's much to recommend her.


00:52:20.432 --> 00:52:23.852
She's rich, young.
They say she's beautiful.


00:52:24.102 --> 00:52:26.063
Yes, and her father betrayed the Crown.


00:52:26.230 --> 00:52:28.148
I make no apologies
for Robert de Thibouville.


00:52:28.398 --> 00:52:31.151
Yeah. Only a shame
he wasn't beheaded for his treason.


00:52:31.401 --> 00:52:34.738
He would have been spared
the sight of this humiliation.


00:52:34.905 --> 00:52:35.906
Gently.


00:52:38.283 --> 00:52:40.536
Yeah. Here, boy.


00:52:40.786 --> 00:52:41.703
Stag's blood.


00:52:44.289 --> 00:52:45.541
Badge of honor.


00:52:46.583 --> 00:52:48.126
Badge of honor.


00:52:48.418 --> 00:52:51.588
Well done, Etienne! Charles.


00:53:00.681 --> 00:53:01.765
What?


00:53:03.308 --> 00:53:04.560
He's suing me.


00:53:04.852 --> 00:53:07.354
Oh. Come in. Take your pants off.


00:53:07.521 --> 00:53:08.564
He's suing me!


00:53:08.772 --> 00:53:10.607
-Who?
-Me!


00:53:10.774 --> 00:53:12.860
For land that is rightfully mine.


00:53:13.193 --> 00:53:16.405
Jean de Carrouges has filed a lawsuit
for a piece of property.


00:53:16.655 --> 00:53:18.448
Why would he sue you
for a piece of property?


00:53:18.991 --> 00:53:21.118
Because you gave it to me.


00:53:21.285 --> 00:53:23.370
He's suing you, too. He's suing us both.


00:53:26.081 --> 00:53:27.791
I fail to see the amusement here, milord.


00:53:28.000 --> 00:53:30.586
How do you sue for that
which was never yours?


00:53:30.752 --> 00:53:31.837
My squire.


00:53:32.379 --> 00:53:36.383
Will you finally submit that I was right
about Jean de Carrouges?


00:53:36.633 --> 00:53:38.594
He's saying he will take the matter
to the king.


00:53:38.802 --> 00:53:40.053
He has bled for this king.


00:53:40.345 --> 00:53:42.097
My cousin, the king.


00:53:42.306 --> 00:53:43.140
Pierre.


00:53:43.307 --> 00:53:46.226
So have I bled. So have you.


00:53:46.393 --> 00:53:48.103
My friend, this matter is settled.


00:53:48.395 --> 00:53:50.230
I'd hoped to surprise you at court.


00:53:50.480 --> 00:53:54.276
Now, you have barged in and cast a pall
over a rather promising evening.


00:53:55.527 --> 00:53:57.154
So, I will tell you now.


00:53:57.321 --> 00:53:59.489
Jean de Carrouges will not be
the new captain at Bellême.


00:53:59.948 --> 00:54:02.242
You will be the new captain at Bellême.


00:54:03.619 --> 00:54:04.620
As if by magic.


00:54:07.581 --> 00:54:09.041
Carrouges will be furious.


00:54:09.291 --> 00:54:11.835
Too true. Now take your fucking pants off.


00:54:13.337 --> 00:54:14.713
Minor delay.


00:54:15.881 --> 00:54:19.134
Who wants to help me
restore my previous state?


00:54:19.301 --> 00:54:20.177
Come here.


00:54:20.552 --> 00:54:23.388
Come down, my boy! Le Gris!


00:54:25.682 --> 00:54:27.935
I will protect this fortress of Bellême...


00:54:28.227 --> 00:54:30.562
and command its garrison as captain...


00:54:30.729 --> 00:54:32.231
to the best of my ability...


00:54:32.523 --> 00:54:35.567
against any and all enemies of my king.


00:54:37.236 --> 00:54:38.320
Jacques Le Gris.


00:54:38.487 --> 00:54:41.782
Captain, rise and be recognized.


00:55:21.280 --> 00:55:22.406
Good day!


00:55:23.740 --> 00:55:25.534
Join us, my squire.


00:55:25.784 --> 00:55:27.411
This is a day for celebration.


00:55:28.328 --> 00:55:30.330
I will not be staying, milord.


00:55:31.039 --> 00:55:33.542
Good God, man,
tell me you're not here to sue me again.


00:55:36.795 --> 00:55:39.381
Mock me, if you may...


00:55:39.548 --> 00:55:42.759
but you cannot change right from wrong
nor wrong from right.


00:55:42.926 --> 00:55:46.471
Enlighten me, my squire,
as to what is right.


00:55:46.638 --> 00:55:50.267
For as I see it, last time you emerged
was to file suit against me...


00:55:50.475 --> 00:55:51.894
for land I lawfully owned...


00:55:52.144 --> 00:55:54.688
and gifted to
my most faithful of squires...


00:55:54.855 --> 00:55:57.274
for services rendered by him unto me.


00:55:57.441 --> 00:56:00.360
What claim could you possibly have had
to this land? You have owned it never.


00:56:00.569 --> 00:56:02.988
I know all about your squire.


00:56:03.155 --> 00:56:06.158
The squire you gifted the land to.


00:56:06.325 --> 00:56:09.703
The one who holds a captaincy now
that is rightfully mine.


00:56:09.912 --> 00:56:10.871
My friend, please.


00:56:11.079 --> 00:56:12.664
-Come, let us talk in private.
-No! No! No!


00:56:12.873 --> 00:56:14.249
I shall be heard!


00:56:14.541 --> 00:56:16.585
I do not accept this!


00:56:16.877 --> 00:56:20.339
My father, for 20 years, my father...


00:56:20.547 --> 00:56:22.508
I've waited for 20 years!


00:56:22.883 --> 00:56:25.719
There's not a nobleman in this hall
who would speak ill of your father.


00:56:25.928 --> 00:56:28.055
You ask for my rents, I yield them up.


00:56:29.181 --> 00:56:30.891
Here, as a man of honor...


00:56:31.308 --> 00:56:33.352
you say I am not the captain?


00:56:33.977 --> 00:56:36.980
You say to me I am not the captain here?


00:56:37.689 --> 00:56:39.566
I say to you whatever I like.


00:56:39.733 --> 00:56:41.610
I decide who is the captain at Bellême.


00:56:42.653 --> 00:56:44.321
That is what you prize.


00:56:44.530 --> 00:56:47.699
That. That sycophant.


00:56:49.409 --> 00:56:51.078
Sycophants all!


00:56:51.245 --> 00:56:53.622
I will sue! I will sue you for this!


00:56:53.830 --> 00:56:55.707
In just three years...


00:56:55.999 --> 00:56:58.919
you've managed to marry
a traitor's daughter...


00:56:59.086 --> 00:57:01.630
sue me for land
that never belonged to you...


00:57:02.130 --> 00:57:04.383
and to stand before me for the second time
in as many years...


00:57:04.591 --> 00:57:06.635
threatening once again to sue...


00:57:06.969 --> 00:57:10.055
all while speaking of duty and honor.


00:57:10.222 --> 00:57:11.598
This is how you serve me?


00:57:12.266 --> 00:57:14.142
I serve the king.


00:57:15.686 --> 00:57:16.937
The king.


00:57:18.397 --> 00:57:19.648
The king.


00:57:21.900 --> 00:57:23.735
Heaven and earth!


00:57:25.988 --> 00:57:27.114
Heaven and earth what?


00:57:58.645 --> 00:58:00.022
14.


00:58:01.106 --> 00:58:03.901
37. 45.


00:58:04.484 --> 00:58:06.653
15. 17 borrowed...


00:58:20.751 --> 00:58:21.919
Come.


00:58:22.628 --> 00:58:23.795
Hello.


00:58:25.172 --> 00:58:27.007
Thought you were asleep, milord.


00:58:27.424 --> 00:58:28.967
Aye, great...


00:58:29.843 --> 00:58:32.262
good friend. No, almost...


00:58:32.971 --> 00:58:37.017
but I spied candlelight,
and I knew it must be you.


00:58:37.267 --> 00:58:39.102
I work better alone.


00:58:40.562 --> 00:58:43.190
You make it hard for a man
to get his work done.


00:58:43.398 --> 00:58:46.443
I came here to tell you
I will not be joining you...


00:58:46.693 --> 00:58:48.320
for Crespin's celebration.


00:58:49.279 --> 00:58:50.405
Milord?


00:58:50.614 --> 00:58:53.367
Too far a ride, too cold.


00:58:53.617 --> 00:58:55.994
We'll stay here and fuck women of our own.


00:58:56.203 --> 00:58:57.329
-No.
-No.


00:58:57.579 --> 00:58:59.957
No, I'm told
Jean de Carrouges will be there.


00:59:00.707 --> 00:59:02.543
It's time to heal this wound.


00:59:03.252 --> 00:59:05.462
He will never change. Why even try?


00:59:05.629 --> 00:59:07.673
Because a feud
between your lordship's vassals...


00:59:07.840 --> 00:59:09.383
brings naught but trouble and distraction.


00:59:09.550 --> 00:59:10.467
Oh, good God.


00:59:10.676 --> 00:59:13.470
And because I once stood godfather
to his late son!


00:59:14.721 --> 00:59:16.765
I once held a place in his heart.


00:59:16.932 --> 00:59:18.308
Do as you must.


00:59:18.934 --> 00:59:21.979
You will get to see the mysterious wife.


00:59:22.229 --> 00:59:27.568
Apparently, he's letting her
out of the dungeon for one time only.


00:59:27.734 --> 00:59:30.404
One can only hope
he hasn't taken away her books.


00:59:32.030 --> 00:59:33.991
Carrouges' wife reads?


00:59:35.033 --> 00:59:37.619
In as many languages as you do,
I'm told.


00:59:38.412 --> 00:59:39.746
Strange match.


00:59:39.997 --> 00:59:41.915
It is. Will wonders never cease?


00:59:42.124 --> 00:59:44.168
-Come to the celebration, milord!
-No.


00:59:44.334 --> 00:59:45.878
-Come!
-No.


00:59:54.970 --> 00:59:56.430
Too much wine. My Latin fails me.


00:59:56.638 --> 00:59:58.974
"We forgive a child afraid of the dark.


00:59:59.224 --> 01:00:02.144
"Tragedy is men afraid of the light."


01:00:04.396 --> 01:00:06.565
Your decency will be the end of you.


01:00:07.149 --> 01:00:09.693
And there is no end to my decency.
No, milord!


01:00:09.860 --> 01:00:11.153
Recalculate!


01:00:14.406 --> 01:00:15.324
Sorry.


01:00:15.824 --> 01:00:16.909
I think you'd enjoy it.


01:00:17.159 --> 01:00:19.703
We will ride from the valley
to where the river ends.


01:00:20.162 --> 01:00:23.415
We could dine there.


01:00:25.334 --> 01:00:27.544
My servants could prepare a picnic.


01:00:27.878 --> 01:00:30.422
Oh, Jacques Le Gris, save your breath.


01:00:30.672 --> 01:00:33.050
I've heard all about you
from the ladies at court.


01:00:33.342 --> 01:00:34.551
They're just boasting.


01:00:34.760 --> 01:00:35.844
Carrouges.


01:00:41.266 --> 01:00:42.518
Pardon me, milady.


01:00:57.282 --> 01:00:58.116
Carrouges.


01:00:59.076 --> 01:01:00.035
Le Gris.


01:01:00.786 --> 01:01:04.331
Pax! Well done! Well done, all!


01:01:04.706 --> 01:01:07.918
Let there be no ill will
among the servants of our king.


01:01:08.168 --> 01:01:09.878
His Majesty needs us all right now.


01:01:10.087 --> 01:01:12.589
Hear, hear. Well spoken.


01:01:13.423 --> 01:01:14.842
Marguerite, come.


01:01:15.384 --> 01:01:16.885
Give my old friend a kiss.


01:01:17.094 --> 01:01:19.221
Show him the good faith
of the house Carrouges.


01:01:28.272 --> 01:01:29.523
Bravo!


01:01:44.288 --> 01:01:45.539
If we...


01:01:47.124 --> 01:01:48.125
There.


01:01:49.001 --> 01:01:52.212
I think... There you go.


01:02:04.683 --> 01:02:07.019
It's a shame we had not met until tonight.


01:02:09.062 --> 01:02:10.480
Is it?


01:02:11.899 --> 01:02:17.446
I had no idea what a lucky man Carrouges
was for having such a beautiful wife.


01:02:19.323 --> 01:02:23.368
From what I have heard, you have
no trouble acquiring beautiful women.


01:02:25.704 --> 01:02:27.539
And from what I have heard...


01:02:27.789 --> 01:02:29.958
we may have a great deal in common.


01:02:30.584 --> 01:02:32.586
What could we possibly have in common?


01:02:33.170 --> 01:02:35.631
Appreciation of one another's
extraordinary good looks.


01:02:41.512 --> 01:02:43.472
You are quite talented
when it comes to flattery.


01:02:43.639 --> 01:02:45.432
I only speak the truth.


01:02:45.641 --> 01:02:46.975
And what else?


01:02:47.226 --> 01:02:48.769
You are a reader?


01:02:54.358 --> 01:02:55.484
Like myself.


01:02:57.236 --> 01:02:58.779
Romance of the Rose.


01:03:00.656 --> 01:03:01.740
I thought it rather dull.


01:03:01.907 --> 01:03:03.659
Dull? The book is wretched.


01:03:06.787 --> 01:03:09.331
I much prefer Percival's Courtesy.


01:03:09.957 --> 01:03:12.918
It's a much more challenging
and interesting novel.


01:03:13.293 --> 01:03:14.962
Smart woman.


01:03:15.128 --> 01:03:16.421
Tell me.


01:03:18.090 --> 01:03:19.967
He is naïve & foolish.


01:03:20.717 --> 01:03:24.096
Yet he is of so pure a heart
he's able to claim the Grail.


01:03:25.222 --> 01:03:26.598
I admire that.


01:03:27.641 --> 01:03:29.184
I understand him.


01:03:29.643 --> 01:03:31.562
He knows what he desires...


01:03:31.812 --> 01:03:34.231
...and doesn't give up
until he attains it.


01:03:36.149 --> 01:03:38.360
Good minds belong together.


01:03:38.694 --> 01:03:40.362
Don't get ahead of yourself.


01:03:45.325 --> 01:03:46.577
Carrouges.


01:03:51.081 --> 01:03:53.333
Your wife charms me, my friend.


01:04:21.904 --> 01:04:24.156
To even think is to covet, my lord.


01:04:25.365 --> 01:04:27.993
No less sinful than her coveting me.


01:05:07.824 --> 01:05:09.785
Please forgive me. I wish...


01:06:01.128 --> 01:06:01.962
Milord?


01:06:16.476 --> 01:06:18.770
I've never seen you like this, milord.


01:06:23.400 --> 01:06:24.735
Nor have I, my friend.


01:06:25.152 --> 01:06:27.654
Word is not promising
on the Scottish front.


01:06:28.864 --> 01:06:30.699
Perhaps the Lady Marguerite's
already a widow.


01:06:31.450 --> 01:06:34.369
I would not wager against
Jean de Carrouges in battle.


01:06:35.454 --> 01:06:38.665
What do you think
her and Jean speak about?


01:06:39.958 --> 01:06:41.710
You think they read together?


01:06:42.544 --> 01:06:44.254
But he's illiterate, though, isn't he?


01:06:46.715 --> 01:06:49.384
The debt we owe to our friends
is the greatest of all.


01:06:49.843 --> 01:06:52.179
Is it greater than love?


01:07:11.949 --> 01:07:14.284
I didn't train him properly.


01:07:14.451 --> 01:07:15.786
The fault is mine.


01:07:16.411 --> 01:07:19.331
My lords! My lords!


01:07:19.498 --> 01:07:23.585
I present the knight,
Sir Jean de Carrouges!


01:07:31.468 --> 01:07:34.763
Milord, I return from the royal campaign
in Scotland to report to you.


01:07:35.931 --> 01:07:37.683
Rise, Sir Knight, speak.


01:07:42.521 --> 01:07:46.441
We found ourselves unwelcome
by our Scottish allies.


01:07:47.109 --> 01:07:48.193
We laid siege at Wark.


01:07:48.402 --> 01:07:51.655
Louder, Sir Knight,
they cannot hear you in the back.


01:07:54.867 --> 01:07:56.910
We laid siege at Wark.


01:07:59.788 --> 01:08:01.331
Milord, I return...


01:08:02.374 --> 01:08:04.835
with neither plunder nor prisoners.


01:08:05.043 --> 01:08:08.547
And without five of the nine squires
under my command.


01:08:10.090 --> 01:08:12.718
Indeed, I return a knight.


01:08:12.885 --> 01:08:15.512
One who curses Scotland
and the hour I set foot there.


01:08:15.762 --> 01:08:16.930
Yes.


01:08:17.598 --> 01:08:19.765
Word had arrived ahead of you...


01:08:19.975 --> 01:08:23.228
of your calamitous campaign.


01:08:23.687 --> 01:08:25.229
A tragic result, Jean...


01:08:25.479 --> 01:08:27.733
though, I dare say,
no fault of your command.


01:08:27.899 --> 01:08:28.901
Hear, hear!


01:08:34.156 --> 01:08:35.782
Where are you off to now, Jean?


01:08:35.948 --> 01:08:37.576
I'm bound for Paris.


01:08:37.743 --> 01:08:39.536
I have business with the treasurer
for my payment.


01:08:39.786 --> 01:08:40.621
Very good.


01:08:40.828 --> 01:08:43.207
A good soldier and good fortune
are not long parted.


01:08:45.042 --> 01:08:47.211
I return a knight.


01:08:47.419 --> 01:08:51.131
That is the second time
you do not call me "sir."


01:08:51.340 --> 01:08:53.258
There will not be a third.


01:09:00.098 --> 01:09:02.142
No offense intended, Sir Jean.


01:09:03.602 --> 01:09:05.604
I will not be patronized...


01:09:07.064 --> 01:09:08.524
by this squire...


01:09:10.192 --> 01:09:12.402
who lies about court...


01:09:12.653 --> 01:09:15.863
waiting to be fêted with gift...


01:09:16.113 --> 01:09:18.450
upon gift upon gift...


01:09:20.327 --> 01:09:21.537
and risks nothing!


01:09:23.121 --> 01:09:24.206
Nothing.


01:09:26.416 --> 01:09:29.795
He may acquire
more property in this world...


01:09:31.380 --> 01:09:32.756
find more favor...


01:09:33.881 --> 01:09:35.801
eat more, drink more...


01:09:36.593 --> 01:09:38.011
bed more...


01:09:38.845 --> 01:09:42.683
and otherwise, call himself a man of arms.


01:09:43.642 --> 01:09:45.477
But in this hall...


01:09:45.685 --> 01:09:47.104
and any other...


01:09:47.312 --> 01:09:49.022
in my company...


01:09:49.231 --> 01:09:50.983
he will call me "sir."


01:09:51.984 --> 01:09:53.193
Sir.


01:09:54.236 --> 01:09:55.195
Sir.


01:09:56.572 --> 01:09:57.990
Indeed...


01:09:58.198 --> 01:09:59.324
good sir.


01:10:02.411 --> 01:10:04.830
Enjoy your time in Paris...


01:10:05.080 --> 01:10:06.081
Sir Jean.


01:10:08.876 --> 01:10:10.377
That is all, Jean.


01:10:17.050 --> 01:10:18.051
Milord.


01:10:34.067 --> 01:10:34.902
Who's there?


01:10:35.068 --> 01:10:39.323
It's I, Adam Louvel, milady.


01:10:39.573 --> 01:10:40.365
Adam Louvel?


01:10:41.658 --> 01:10:43.660
I'm ashamed to have to ask a great favor.


01:10:45.537 --> 01:10:48.290
My horse has thrown a shoe and...


01:10:48.540 --> 01:10:49.625
Nobody's here.


01:10:49.791 --> 01:10:51.210
I'm not permitted to open the door.


01:10:51.376 --> 01:10:52.586
No, of course.


01:10:52.920 --> 01:10:56.882
I just wondered if I could come inside
and warm myself while he's reshod.


01:10:57.090 --> 01:10:59.551
I'm so sorry to have to ask.


01:11:00.052 --> 01:11:02.846
For a moment. I hate to ask.


01:11:10.604 --> 01:11:12.397
Milady, forgive me for intruding.


01:11:14.983 --> 01:11:18.028
I love you more than any other,
and I would do anything for you.


01:11:18.195 --> 01:11:20.280
Everything I have is yours.


01:11:21.365 --> 01:11:23.325
How can you speak to me like this?


01:11:23.659 --> 01:11:26.662
Marguerite, what way then
would I speak to you?


01:11:26.828 --> 01:11:29.456
Milady, you must know it cannot be helped.


01:11:29.706 --> 01:11:32.376
My love for you has consumed me.


01:11:32.543 --> 01:11:33.544
How dare you?


01:11:33.794 --> 01:11:35.712
Milady, when milord sets his course
for love...


01:11:35.879 --> 01:11:36.505
Do not speak!


01:11:36.672 --> 01:11:38.257
You must leave now. Please.


01:11:38.423 --> 01:11:39.925
You heard the lady. Leave us!


01:11:40.092 --> 01:11:41.009
Milord.


01:11:47.933 --> 01:11:50.143
-I am married.
-Yes.


01:11:50.310 --> 01:11:52.354
You are saddled with a terrible burden.


01:11:53.105 --> 01:11:56.400
A cold, callous man
who does not love you as I do.


01:11:56.608 --> 01:11:58.402
Who cannot appreciate you
for the marvel that you are.


01:11:58.610 --> 01:12:00.237
-Please.
-I only want for your happiness.


01:12:00.404 --> 01:12:02.614
I cannot bear to see you in such hardship.


01:12:02.823 --> 01:12:05.075
I know your house's finances are fragile.


01:12:05.242 --> 01:12:06.660
My lord provides for me.


01:12:06.869 --> 01:12:07.911
Yes.


01:12:11.331 --> 01:12:14.084
But does he know you to be the most...


01:12:15.002 --> 01:12:16.461
exquisite...


01:12:19.047 --> 01:12:20.757
fascinating woman?


01:12:24.052 --> 01:12:25.762
A woman...


01:12:26.847 --> 01:12:28.473
I would devote my whole life to.


01:12:31.643 --> 01:12:34.396
Oh, hear me say I'm in love with you.


01:12:34.605 --> 01:12:36.732
I know you love me, too. You must.


01:12:36.940 --> 01:12:39.026
You must leave. Now, please.


01:13:20.025 --> 01:13:21.610
Jeanette!


01:13:27.991 --> 01:13:30.827
If you run, I will only chase you.


01:13:42.756 --> 01:13:43.674
-No.
-Yes.


01:13:43.841 --> 01:13:44.925
No.


01:13:47.010 --> 01:13:48.428
No.


01:13:53.100 --> 01:13:54.184
No.


01:13:56.395 --> 01:13:57.396
No!


01:14:25.674 --> 01:14:26.675
No.


01:14:30.179 --> 01:14:31.180
No.


01:14:32.514 --> 01:14:33.849
Please, no.


01:15:27.653 --> 01:15:30.656
You fear yourself guilty, but, my love...


01:15:30.822 --> 01:15:33.033
I beseech you, tell no one.


01:15:35.160 --> 01:15:37.079
For your own safety.


01:15:37.871 --> 01:15:40.082
If your husband hears of this...


01:15:41.166 --> 01:15:42.334
he may kill you.


01:15:43.710 --> 01:15:45.254
Say nothing.


01:15:47.214 --> 01:15:49.341
I will keep quiet, too.


01:15:56.765 --> 01:15:59.184
Do not feel badly, my love.


01:16:00.394 --> 01:16:02.729
We could not help ourselves.


01:16:08.735 --> 01:16:10.863
Forgive me, Father, for I have sinned.


01:16:11.071 --> 01:16:12.656
Speak, my son.


01:16:13.782 --> 01:16:16.702
I carry a sin
that weighs heavy upon my heart.


01:16:16.869 --> 01:16:18.328
What is it, my son?


01:16:19.872 --> 01:16:22.291
I have committed the sin of adultery...


01:16:24.042 --> 01:16:26.712
against a man I once considered a friend.


01:16:27.504 --> 01:16:28.505
You know your commandments?


01:16:28.672 --> 01:16:30.382
Yes, Father.


01:16:31.049 --> 01:16:32.801
I ask forgiveness.


01:16:33.051 --> 01:16:34.803
My son, Matthew tells us...


01:16:35.554 --> 01:16:37.556
everyone who looks at a woman with lust...


01:16:37.764 --> 01:16:40.392
has already committed adultery
with her in his heart.


01:16:40.601 --> 01:16:42.519
But is love a sin, Father?


01:16:44.479 --> 01:16:46.190
How can I seek absolution for love?


01:16:46.356 --> 01:16:47.900
This is the work of the Devil.


01:16:48.066 --> 01:16:49.902
This temptress leads you astray.


01:16:50.110 --> 01:16:52.654
Just as Eve lured Adam
from the divine path.


01:16:52.821 --> 01:16:53.947
That is not love.


01:16:54.156 --> 01:16:56.200
Then why?


01:16:57.576 --> 01:16:59.995
God is faithful.


01:17:00.162 --> 01:17:04.124
He will not let you be tempted
beyond what you can bear.


01:17:05.584 --> 01:17:07.336
This is a test.


01:17:10.255 --> 01:17:11.298
-My friend.
-Milord.


01:17:12.007 --> 01:17:13.008
Sit.


01:17:21.475 --> 01:17:23.185
You will need to sit.


01:17:27.689 --> 01:17:28.524
Drink this.


01:17:35.239 --> 01:17:38.075
You should drink all of it.


01:17:43.247 --> 01:17:45.999
There is no other way to say this
than to speak plainly.


01:17:47.584 --> 01:17:51.964
A most unspeakable charge
has been brought against you.


01:17:53.090 --> 01:17:56.051
Jean de Carrouges evidently...


01:17:56.218 --> 01:17:57.553
among others...


01:17:57.719 --> 01:18:00.472
has been telling any and all
who will listen...


01:18:00.639 --> 01:18:02.140
that you...


01:18:03.934 --> 01:18:07.271
took his wife against her will.


01:18:16.154 --> 01:18:17.364
I know not what to say.


01:18:19.992 --> 01:18:21.827
Why would she say that?


01:18:22.619 --> 01:18:25.873
Jacques, it is you and I here.


01:18:26.039 --> 01:18:28.208
I must know. This is a serious matter.


01:18:29.251 --> 01:18:30.961
The accusation is false.


01:18:35.090 --> 01:18:38.385
Of course, she made the customary protest,
but she is a lady.


01:18:38.552 --> 01:18:40.304
It was not against her will.


01:18:44.099 --> 01:18:46.643
Why would I ever need to do that?


01:18:46.852 --> 01:18:49.104
Have you ever known me
to lack the company of women?


01:18:49.396 --> 01:18:50.731
No.


01:18:50.981 --> 01:18:53.525
But you have not been yourself of late.


01:18:54.568 --> 01:18:57.946
It is true, I confess,
it is a feeling I've never had before.


01:18:58.113 --> 01:18:59.448
A love...


01:19:02.034 --> 01:19:03.160
that I've never known.


01:19:06.330 --> 01:19:09.666
It's taken all my strength
not to return to her.


01:19:12.711 --> 01:19:13.712
We knew it was wrong...


01:19:13.921 --> 01:19:16.423
I confessed my adultery,
and performed my penance.


01:19:16.632 --> 01:19:19.635
But I swear to you,
this charge of rape is false.


01:19:20.260 --> 01:19:22.721
Of course it's absurd.
It's as I suspected.


01:19:22.930 --> 01:19:24.932
But I must defend my name.


01:19:25.098 --> 01:19:26.892
No, you must do no such thing.


01:19:27.100 --> 01:19:28.727
On my honor, I will, milord. I must.


01:19:28.894 --> 01:19:31.980
I know you yearn to defend your name
and your honor...


01:19:32.147 --> 01:19:35.984
but the common mind has no capacity
for this sort of nuance.


01:19:36.818 --> 01:19:38.737
They simply don't understand the world
as we do.


01:19:38.904 --> 01:19:41.114
They see villains and heroes,
that is all.


01:19:41.281 --> 01:19:42.157
Milord...


01:19:42.407 --> 01:19:44.368
Deny, deny, deny.


01:19:44.535 --> 01:19:48.121
Everywhere, always, at all times,
and to all men.


01:19:48.372 --> 01:19:50.040
You did not commit adultery.


01:19:50.207 --> 01:19:51.291
It never happened.


01:19:51.458 --> 01:19:53.126
There is no proof.


01:19:53.961 --> 01:19:56.630
It will always be your word
against that of Jean de Carrouges.


01:19:56.839 --> 01:19:58.006
Yes, milord.


01:19:59.716 --> 01:20:02.177
Of course we will have to endure
a public trial...


01:20:02.386 --> 01:20:05.848
charges of rape
will be brought against you...


01:20:06.640 --> 01:20:09.601
and a verdict will be rendered
by your overlord...


01:20:09.810 --> 01:20:11.854
adjudicating this matter who...


01:20:12.062 --> 01:20:14.356
as the fates would have it...


01:20:14.523 --> 01:20:16.233
happens to be me.


01:20:22.489 --> 01:20:26.702
I hereby find said Jacques Le Gris
to be completely innocent...


01:20:26.869 --> 01:20:28.662
and wholly without guilt.


01:20:28.871 --> 01:20:31.373
I order the criminal complaint annulled...


01:20:31.582 --> 01:20:33.500
and stricken from the record.


01:20:33.667 --> 01:20:36.086
Let there be
no further questions about it.


01:20:36.879 --> 01:20:38.922
Let there be no more gossip...


01:20:39.089 --> 01:20:41.967
the penalty a punishment by my hand.


01:20:42.301 --> 01:20:43.802
Is that understood?


01:20:44.428 --> 01:20:47.598
As to the sworn testimony
of Lady Marguerite...


01:20:47.764 --> 01:20:51.018
one can only come to the conclusion
she must have dreamt it.


01:20:51.977 --> 01:20:54.813
Now, have these findings
sent immediately to Paris...


01:20:55.022 --> 01:20:58.859
before this insouciant knight troubles
our king any further with this nonsense.


01:21:00.777 --> 01:21:01.862
Yes, speak.


01:21:02.070 --> 01:21:04.198
Milord, I have been informed...


01:21:04.406 --> 01:21:07.492
that Jean de Carrouges
has already travelled to Paris.


01:21:07.659 --> 01:21:11.288
He is filing an appeal to His Majesty
at this very moment.


01:21:19.880 --> 01:21:21.507
Cunt.


01:21:21.715 --> 01:21:23.509
The benefit of clergy.


01:21:23.717 --> 01:21:25.594
There really is no decision to make.


01:21:25.802 --> 01:21:27.596
You're a cleric in minor orders.


01:21:27.763 --> 01:21:30.641
So, you can escape the jurisdiction
of the secular courts...


01:21:30.807 --> 01:21:32.392
and be tried by the Church...


01:21:32.559 --> 01:21:35.062
where conditions are more favorable.


01:21:36.647 --> 01:21:38.440
Men holding church office...


01:21:38.649 --> 01:21:42.444
number disproportionately
among those accused of rape.


01:21:42.694 --> 01:21:46.657
They escape serious punishment
by claiming benefit of clergy, so...


01:21:46.907 --> 01:21:49.993
we'll have the church try your case
and be done with the matter.


01:21:50.285 --> 01:21:52.162
But what of my name?


01:21:55.457 --> 01:21:56.792
Was there...


01:21:57.668 --> 01:21:58.794
an affair?


01:22:01.380 --> 01:22:02.506
Absolutely not.


01:22:02.714 --> 01:22:06.552
It's strange she would claim rape
and risk her life.


01:22:08.220 --> 01:22:10.138
Why would she do this?


01:22:10.305 --> 01:22:14.351
All of France is talking about this,
and I'm innocent.


01:22:14.518 --> 01:22:17.396
I've said publicly
that this never happened!


01:22:17.563 --> 01:22:19.690
And yet, under extraordinary pressure


01:22:19.773 --> 01:22:22.150
and at great risk to her name
and reputation...


01:22:22.401 --> 01:22:25.654
Lady Marguerite has said that it did.


01:22:29.575 --> 01:22:31.577
Formally, this is not about her.


01:22:33.036 --> 01:22:34.538
Rape is not a crime against a woman.


01:22:34.746 --> 01:22:37.916
It is a property crime
against her male guardian.


01:22:38.125 --> 01:22:39.918
In this case, Jean de Carrouges.


01:22:40.127 --> 01:22:44.840
This is not a matter over which a duel
should be fought to the death.


01:22:46.675 --> 01:22:49.052
It should be settled quietly.


01:22:54.016 --> 01:22:55.893
Take the benefit of clergy.


01:22:58.520 --> 01:23:00.189
I'm not a coward.


01:23:10.032 --> 01:23:13.744
Most excellent and powerful king
and our sovereign lord...


01:23:13.911 --> 01:23:15.287
I present myself...


01:23:15.454 --> 01:23:17.289
Jacques Le Gris...


01:23:17.456 --> 01:23:20.918
squire and defendant...


01:23:21.168 --> 01:23:23.170
and I do hereby deny...


01:23:23.420 --> 01:23:24.963
all the aforesaid charges...


01:23:25.130 --> 01:23:26.632
especially...


01:23:27.591 --> 01:23:29.718
of Jean de Carrouges...


01:23:29.927 --> 01:23:32.054
that I did unlawfully...


01:23:34.264 --> 01:23:35.641
and carnally...


01:23:35.849 --> 01:23:37.267
know his wife...


01:23:37.684 --> 01:23:39.770
the Lady Marguerite de Carrouges...


01:23:41.063 --> 01:23:43.148
in the third week of January last...


01:23:43.732 --> 01:23:46.151
or at any other time.


01:23:46.318 --> 01:23:49.279
And I further maintain,
saving the honor of Your Majesty...


01:23:49.905 --> 01:23:51.281
that the said knight...


01:23:51.490 --> 01:23:53.242
has falsely...


01:23:53.450 --> 01:23:54.910
and wickedly lied!


01:23:56.578 --> 01:23:57.955
And that he is false...


01:23:58.455 --> 01:24:00.958
and wicked to say this thing.


01:24:03.669 --> 01:24:05.587
And I further maintain...


01:24:08.298 --> 01:24:10.175
and with the aid of God...


01:24:11.760 --> 01:24:13.303
and with Our Lady...


01:24:15.222 --> 01:24:19.101
I pledge to do whatever is necessary
to prove my innocence.


01:24:33.198 --> 01:24:35.617
The knight and the squire
have spoken well.


01:24:37.202 --> 01:24:39.538
It is ordered now
that the parties present the affidavits...


01:24:39.705 --> 01:24:43.542
which, the court having received,
will render a verdict upon in a fortnight.


01:24:44.877 --> 01:24:46.670
If either man...


01:24:46.879 --> 01:24:48.589
attempts to flee Paris...


01:24:48.797 --> 01:24:51.884
it will be taken as a sign of his guilt.


01:24:52.050 --> 01:24:54.845
Orders will be issued
for his summary arrest...


01:24:56.138 --> 01:24:58.307
and he will be hanged.


01:25:07.357 --> 01:25:11.945
The king will decide
if a duel should indeed be fought.


01:25:18.410 --> 01:25:20.495
What now?


01:25:34.635 --> 01:25:38.722
You will have 330 livres in coin,
furnishings, cloth, and jewels...


01:25:38.931 --> 01:25:42.017
in addition to the estate
at Mont a Gudot as well as...


01:25:42.184 --> 01:25:43.852
And what of Aunou-le-Faucon?


01:25:45.938 --> 01:25:49.858
I was forced to sell that property
to Count Pierre.


01:25:57.115 --> 01:26:00.827
You and I agreed this land should be
assumed by whomever marries your daughter.


01:26:04.581 --> 01:26:06.250
Is this not part of the dowry?


01:26:06.458 --> 01:26:08.252
I was unable to pay my rents.


01:26:08.418 --> 01:26:09.795
You promised me.


01:26:10.337 --> 01:26:12.047
We discussed this.


01:26:12.840 --> 01:26:14.591
My daughter comes with the money
and the land that I've offered.


01:26:14.758 --> 01:26:16.468
That is all that I own.


01:26:18.387 --> 01:26:20.848
And what of the bride price?


01:26:21.265 --> 01:26:25.561
I offer you a name of value.


01:26:35.320 --> 01:26:40.158
I should expect she's capable
of performing her wifely duties?


01:26:40.325 --> 01:26:41.326
Bearing an heir.


01:26:42.202 --> 01:26:44.621
My daughter is strong and healthy...


01:26:45.289 --> 01:26:47.499
and ready to honor the marriage.


01:26:49.626 --> 01:26:53.380
The conception of an heir
and children to follow shall be swift.


01:26:54.590 --> 01:26:56.425
And prolific.


01:27:03.390 --> 01:27:04.433
Proceed.


01:27:06.685 --> 01:27:08.353
The wedding will proceed!


01:27:34.880 --> 01:27:36.298
You're perfect.


01:28:01.031 --> 01:28:03.283
I hope this was pleasurable for you.


01:28:05.994 --> 01:28:07.871
Yes, milord, very.


01:28:09.331 --> 01:28:13.669
I could not have asked
for a more satisfying wedding night.


01:28:15.087 --> 01:28:18.715
Perhaps we have conceived
on this very night.


01:28:33.272 --> 01:28:35.190
I think you would enjoy it.
We will ride...


01:28:35.357 --> 01:28:37.818
-from the valley to where the river...
-Milord. Carrouges.


01:28:51.790 --> 01:28:52.791
Carrouges.


01:28:54.251 --> 01:28:55.252
Le Gris.


01:28:55.836 --> 01:28:59.131
Pax! Well done! Well done, all!


01:28:59.298 --> 01:29:02.301
Let there be no ill will
between servants of our king.


01:29:03.343 --> 01:29:05.304
Marguerite, come.


01:29:05.470 --> 01:29:09.391
Give my old friend a kiss. Show him
the good faith of the house Carrouges.


01:29:29.077 --> 01:29:32.247
Who is that squire?
He's dangerously handsome.


01:29:32.414 --> 01:29:34.750
He has quite the reputation.


01:29:34.917 --> 01:29:36.460
Should milord not return from battle,


01:29:36.543 --> 01:29:37.878
I would happily strengthen
that reputation.


01:29:38.045 --> 01:29:39.630
I think that could be arranged regardless.


01:29:39.796 --> 01:29:42.299
-Marie.
-How can you speak like this?


01:29:42.466 --> 01:29:44.760
I should not be seen nor heard with you.


01:29:45.052 --> 01:29:46.595
My husband would have my head.


01:29:46.762 --> 01:29:48.722
But you would die happy.


01:29:48.889 --> 01:29:50.682
He's handsome.


01:29:50.849 --> 01:29:52.434
Charming, I hear.


01:29:52.601 --> 01:29:55.229
True, he is handsome and charming...


01:29:55.395 --> 01:29:57.689
but my husband does not trust him.


01:30:04.780 --> 01:30:06.031
I am proud of you.


01:30:06.823 --> 01:30:09.243
I know that this reconciliation
must have been difficult.


01:30:09.576 --> 01:30:11.245
You gave me good counsel.


01:30:12.246 --> 01:30:14.039
You are kind to Jacques Le Gris.


01:30:14.915 --> 01:30:17.167
That man is unduly fond of himself.


01:30:18.919 --> 01:30:20.420
But you see...


01:30:20.838 --> 01:30:24.716
how a smile and a kind word
go much further than a threat.


01:30:26.051 --> 01:30:27.469
Even if you don't mean it.


01:30:33.308 --> 01:30:34.977
While I'm gone...


01:30:35.185 --> 01:30:36.812
besides a bountiful harvest...


01:30:36.979 --> 01:30:39.940
our fortunes will turn most
on the breeding of these horses.


01:30:40.148 --> 01:30:42.067
And the collection of rents?


01:30:42.276 --> 01:30:43.777
Yes, of course.


01:30:43.944 --> 01:30:45.779
Stand over there.


01:30:45.946 --> 01:30:47.990
I bought this mare for breeding.


01:30:48.198 --> 01:30:51.243
Comes from a long line of war horses.


01:30:51.743 --> 01:30:54.580
She will foal many a valuable colt.


01:30:54.788 --> 01:30:55.789
Sometimes, the difference...


01:30:55.998 --> 01:30:59.918
between victory and defeat,
between life and death...


01:31:00.127 --> 01:31:02.546
Get out of the way!
Get out of the way!


01:31:02.713 --> 01:31:03.797
Mind the gate!


01:31:05.465 --> 01:31:06.550
No!


01:31:07.301 --> 01:31:08.051
Steady!


01:31:09.553 --> 01:31:10.262
No!


01:31:10.429 --> 01:31:11.388
Steady, girl.


01:31:13.015 --> 01:31:14.099
-Easy! Easy!
-Get hold of her.


01:31:14.766 --> 01:31:16.101
Not the stallion!


01:31:17.436 --> 01:31:19.062
No! Not you!


01:31:19.313 --> 01:31:20.814
Not with my mare!


01:31:24.818 --> 01:31:26.862
The gates remain closed!


01:31:27.029 --> 01:31:28.363
Yes, milord.


01:31:29.573 --> 01:31:31.200
The mare is in season!


01:31:32.868 --> 01:31:35.078
These are not trifling matters.


01:31:35.329 --> 01:31:36.413
It costs money.


01:31:40.667 --> 01:31:44.171
Nothing would get done around here
were it not for me.


01:32:10.280 --> 01:32:14.368
I trust your little death
was a memorable and a productive one.


01:32:14.826 --> 01:32:16.620
It was like none other.


01:32:24.628 --> 01:32:27.089
Why have I not yet conceived?


01:32:29.633 --> 01:32:31.927
I want a child so very badly.


01:32:32.469 --> 01:32:34.638
Wanting a child has nothing to do
with the matter, Marguerite.


01:32:34.805 --> 01:32:36.515
We need a son.


01:32:38.392 --> 01:32:41.353
You think I do not know this?


01:32:41.520 --> 01:32:43.105
I think of nothing else.


01:32:43.355 --> 01:32:46.275
I did not have this problem
with my first wife.


01:32:50.195 --> 01:32:52.197
I shall return in a few months.


01:32:52.447 --> 01:32:55.075
You will be safe here with my mother
and your servants.


01:32:55.576 --> 01:32:57.494
You must never allow yourself
to be unattended.


01:32:59.079 --> 01:33:01.331
And do not look so sad.


01:33:01.623 --> 01:33:05.294
I prefer you to be in good spirits
as I go off to war.


01:33:05.460 --> 01:33:08.172
I'm proud of you, milord.


01:33:11.175 --> 01:33:12.467
You will take care of the estate.


01:33:12.718 --> 01:33:14.136
See that it does not fall into disarray.


01:33:14.344 --> 01:33:16.096
Of course.


01:33:28.567 --> 01:33:29.610
-Good morning.
-Milady.


01:33:29.818 --> 01:33:30.986
-Milady.
-Good morning.


01:33:31.278 --> 01:33:33.238
Good morning, Henri.


01:33:33.488 --> 01:33:35.490
Good morning to you, milady.


01:33:36.116 --> 01:33:37.826
The pregnancy seems to be going well.


01:33:39.411 --> 01:33:41.038
Yes, milady.


01:33:41.288 --> 01:33:42.789
So why is she penned up?


01:33:44.374 --> 01:33:47.252
Before my master left,
he had told me to do so.


01:33:49.922 --> 01:33:53.091
My husband knows much about horses...


01:33:53.300 --> 01:33:55.052
riding them.


01:33:55.260 --> 01:33:56.845
The upbringing, I leave to you.


01:33:59.556 --> 01:34:02.476
It would be better for the health
of the mare to be roaming free.


01:34:03.435 --> 01:34:05.938
Then she shall roam free.


01:34:06.104 --> 01:34:07.523
Thank you, milady.


01:34:14.112 --> 01:34:18.242
This is last month's rent as well, milady.


01:34:18.408 --> 01:34:19.660
Were you unable to pay?


01:34:20.577 --> 01:34:22.913
Your lord never came to collect it.


01:34:28.544 --> 01:34:30.796
-Is this unusual?
-No.


01:34:31.338 --> 01:34:33.048
But it is no trouble.


01:34:34.675 --> 01:34:36.343
Thank you.


01:34:52.067 --> 01:34:53.694
Henri?


01:34:54.069 --> 01:34:55.404
Yes, milady?


01:34:56.738 --> 01:34:59.408
Are the oxen not too slow?


01:34:59.658 --> 01:35:01.869
The thaw came late this year.


01:35:02.077 --> 01:35:03.412
It's been hard going for them.


01:35:03.787 --> 01:35:07.249
If we are to sow the oats in time
for harvest, then we must be much faster.


01:35:07.416 --> 01:35:08.542
I should like to use the horses.


01:35:09.793 --> 01:35:12.171
Yes, but we never use the horses
for that purpose.


01:35:12.379 --> 01:35:13.964
My master feels they are too valuable.


01:35:14.131 --> 01:35:18.385
They will be of no value
if they starve to death this winter.


01:35:18.677 --> 01:35:19.720
See that it's done.


01:35:20.470 --> 01:35:21.555
Right away.


01:35:24.850 --> 01:35:27.477
I see you have
some sun on your face, milady.


01:35:27.644 --> 01:35:29.104
-You look well.
-Do I?


01:35:29.313 --> 01:35:31.148
I prefer not to be pink.


01:35:31.315 --> 01:35:32.482
Though it was a lovely day.


01:35:33.025 --> 01:35:35.736
A little color on one's face
proves they're alive.


01:35:36.570 --> 01:35:37.738
Barely.


01:35:37.946 --> 01:35:39.531
Have you heard we've a famous tailor


01:35:39.615 --> 01:35:41.909
from Paris arriving
in the village next week?


01:35:42.117 --> 01:35:45.913
You've been working hard,
why not buy yourself a new dress?


01:35:46.580 --> 01:35:47.706
Oh, I don't know.


01:35:47.915 --> 01:35:50.125
He copies the dresses
Queen Isabeau's been seen wearing.


01:35:50.334 --> 01:35:51.335
They're quite the rage.


01:35:51.543 --> 01:35:52.669
I have seen those.


01:35:52.878 --> 01:35:54.254
The neckline is very low.


01:35:54.505 --> 01:35:58.759
Almost so low that one might see
the queen's pierced nipples.


01:35:59.092 --> 01:36:00.010
She does not.


01:36:00.219 --> 01:36:01.637
-She does.
-She does not...


01:36:03.305 --> 01:36:04.640
Good evening.


01:36:05.849 --> 01:36:07.226
Good evening.


01:36:11.605 --> 01:36:14.066
Things seem to be running quite well.


01:36:14.900 --> 01:36:17.277
I enjoy doing these tasks.


01:36:17.486 --> 01:36:19.404
It's my pleasure.


01:36:19.571 --> 01:36:21.073
Until he returns from Scotland...


01:36:21.281 --> 01:36:22.616
of course.


01:36:23.617 --> 01:36:24.910
It is unfortunate, however...


01:36:25.118 --> 01:36:26.578
that you've not been capable of


01:36:26.662 --> 01:36:29.581
steering your husband away
from conflict with others.


01:36:29.790 --> 01:36:32.709
Jean does what he feels is necessary.


01:36:35.671 --> 01:36:38.549
May I ask what you're making?
It looks lovely.


01:36:40.634 --> 01:36:42.010
I say with sorrow...


01:36:42.219 --> 01:36:43.804
something...


01:36:44.054 --> 01:36:46.807
apparently fruitless.


01:36:48.308 --> 01:36:50.602
You are very cruel.


01:36:53.021 --> 01:36:54.064
I am a good wife.


01:36:55.274 --> 01:36:58.277
As long as you are fulfilling
your wifely duties.


01:37:01.446 --> 01:37:04.533
Or perhaps you cannot be pleased.


01:37:15.043 --> 01:37:16.503
How is your sleep?


01:37:16.712 --> 01:37:17.963
Often interrupted.


01:37:18.422 --> 01:37:20.674
Flaccid joints.


01:37:21.383 --> 01:37:24.094
Bitter taste in the mouth?


01:37:24.261 --> 01:37:25.721
I don't know.


01:37:27.931 --> 01:37:32.811
My lady, it appears you are suffering
from an imbalance of the four humors...


01:37:33.020 --> 01:37:35.856
primarily black bile.


01:37:36.106 --> 01:37:37.524
You are severely melancholic...


01:37:37.733 --> 01:37:41.278
your body is cold and dry.


01:37:41.612 --> 01:37:42.654
Perhaps this...


01:37:42.863 --> 01:37:45.532
combined with various other factors...


01:37:45.699 --> 01:37:47.201
including God's will...


01:37:47.451 --> 01:37:49.578
could be preventing conception.


01:37:53.165 --> 01:37:56.668
It is imperative
that you have a pleasurable conclusion...


01:37:56.835 --> 01:37:59.713
similar to your husband's,
in order to conceive a child.


01:38:00.214 --> 01:38:01.048
You achieve this?


01:38:02.132 --> 01:38:03.967
Yes.


01:38:04.426 --> 01:38:08.222
You find intercourse with your husband
pleasurable?


01:38:09.431 --> 01:38:11.225
Yes, of course, Doctor.


01:38:13.435 --> 01:38:16.355
Although I am not certain
I am experiencing


01:38:16.438 --> 01:38:18.732
"the little death," as they say.


01:38:19.066 --> 01:38:22.694
But if you find it pleasurable,
then you are.


01:38:23.946 --> 01:38:25.364
Very well.


01:38:26.198 --> 01:38:27.908
When Jean returns, he shall be grateful...


01:38:28.075 --> 01:38:32.371
as I have put the books in order,
as well as everything else.


01:38:32.621 --> 01:38:35.123
Perhaps he won't mind the expense.


01:38:35.290 --> 01:38:37.251
Let us both get dresses.


01:38:37.417 --> 01:38:39.253
Surprise your new husband.


01:38:39.461 --> 01:38:40.838
He would not approve.


01:38:41.046 --> 01:38:43.257
He would say I have enough dresses.


01:38:44.508 --> 01:38:45.676
I've only been married a short time...


01:38:45.884 --> 01:38:47.594
yet I now understand
the burden of this arrangement.


01:38:47.803 --> 01:38:48.846
You are a newlywed.


01:38:49.054 --> 01:38:50.347
Surely you do not feel burdened.


01:38:50.556 --> 01:38:51.807
Bernard is a frugal man...


01:38:52.015 --> 01:38:54.101
and he does not like to kiss me.


01:38:56.812 --> 01:38:58.689
I once thought his appearance
would become more pleasing...


01:38:58.897 --> 01:39:01.108
but, instead, it's become more repulsive.


01:39:02.276 --> 01:39:04.528
So I suppose I am relieved...


01:39:04.695 --> 01:39:05.737
about the kissing.


01:39:08.657 --> 01:39:11.243
He is not like Jean,
handsome and generous.


01:39:11.869 --> 01:39:14.496
My marriage is not without its problems.


01:39:25.090 --> 01:39:26.717
I shall be right with you, ladies.


01:39:26.884 --> 01:39:28.177
Thank you.


01:40:00.292 --> 01:40:04.087
Despite Le Gris'
many deplorable qualities...


01:40:04.296 --> 01:40:06.423
one cannot be blind to his appearance.


01:40:06.632 --> 01:40:07.633
Crude as he is.


01:40:07.799 --> 01:40:09.259
Offensive as well.


01:40:10.636 --> 01:40:12.596
They're all such fools.


01:40:14.306 --> 01:40:15.849
Agreed.


01:40:31.406 --> 01:40:32.991
Welcome back, sire.


01:40:42.876 --> 01:40:44.294
Welcome home, my love.


01:41:07.192 --> 01:41:08.861
I am so happy to see you.


01:41:09.027 --> 01:41:11.071
My God, Marguerite...


01:41:11.238 --> 01:41:12.865
have you lost your dignity?


01:41:15.242 --> 01:41:19.079
Go upstairs
before the others think you a harlot.


01:41:20.664 --> 01:41:22.499
I am your wife.


01:41:33.427 --> 01:41:37.306
Welcome home, my courageous son.


01:41:38.015 --> 01:41:39.308
Thank you.


01:41:39.474 --> 01:41:41.685
Had I seen the gown
or known it was being made...


01:41:41.894 --> 01:41:42.895
I would've stopped it.


01:41:47.107 --> 01:41:49.318
And how would you have done that
in my household?


01:41:49.484 --> 01:41:50.861
I wonder.


01:41:51.278 --> 01:41:54.239
Are you gonna let your wife speak to me
in a tone like this?


01:41:55.199 --> 01:41:57.367
Marguerite is a grown woman, Mother.


01:41:57.576 --> 01:41:59.036
The decisions she makes are her own.


01:41:59.870 --> 01:42:01.663
As well as the lessons learned.


01:42:05.459 --> 01:42:07.794
Tomorrow I must go to Paris.


01:42:08.003 --> 01:42:09.129
I'll be away one week.


01:42:09.296 --> 01:42:12.174
But you are ill.
You must stay here, indoors.


01:42:12.341 --> 01:42:13.717
Yes, please stay.


01:42:13.884 --> 01:42:14.885
I'm owed money.


01:42:16.261 --> 01:42:18.055
-I intend to collect it.
-Of course.


01:42:19.181 --> 01:42:21.808
Perhaps you may visit some old friends.


01:42:21.975 --> 01:42:24.895
Le Gris is in Argentan.


01:42:25.062 --> 01:42:27.189
Why Le Gris?


01:42:30.442 --> 01:42:33.403
Please ensure Alice is with her
while I'm away.


01:42:34.446 --> 01:42:36.323
I forbid you from leaving the grounds.


01:42:37.616 --> 01:42:39.159
It's not safe.


01:42:41.495 --> 01:42:44.331
I should like to see my friends.


01:42:44.540 --> 01:42:46.208
We're so isolated.


01:42:46.500 --> 01:42:48.043
Precisely.


01:43:05.519 --> 01:43:07.729
-Are you leaving?
-Yes.


01:43:07.938 --> 01:43:09.189
Well, when will you return?


01:43:09.648 --> 01:43:11.608
When my tasks are completed.


01:43:11.775 --> 01:43:12.985
Before nightfall.


01:43:13.694 --> 01:43:16.113
Jean insisted I not be left alone.
You heard him.


01:43:17.322 --> 01:43:18.323
Antoine!


01:43:30.210 --> 01:43:31.420
Sow!


01:43:33.297 --> 01:43:35.048
Eight, nine, 10, 11, 12...


01:43:44.224 --> 01:43:45.893
Stay.


01:43:54.151 --> 01:43:55.777
Who is there?


01:43:55.986 --> 01:43:57.863
It is I.


01:43:58.071 --> 01:44:00.616
Adam Louvel, milady.


01:44:03.619 --> 01:44:05.162
Adam Louvel?


01:44:09.249 --> 01:44:10.250
Hello.


01:44:11.793 --> 01:44:14.254
I have a great favor to ask.


01:44:14.463 --> 01:44:16.673
My horse has thrown a shoe.


01:44:16.965 --> 01:44:18.926
Nobody is here.
I am not permitted to open the door.


01:44:19.092 --> 01:44:20.969
Of course. I understand.


01:44:21.136 --> 01:44:22.554
If I could...


01:44:22.763 --> 01:44:24.765
Could I wait inside while he's reshod?


01:44:24.973 --> 01:44:27.059
Just to warm myself for a moment.


01:44:27.267 --> 01:44:28.894
Will not be long at all.


01:44:29.770 --> 01:44:31.271
It's just an inconvenience.


01:44:31.480 --> 01:44:33.232
-I'm so sorry to have to ask.
-Please.


01:44:36.860 --> 01:44:38.028
Oh, I'm not alone.


01:44:40.072 --> 01:44:43.200
Milady, forgive me for intruding.


01:44:55.087 --> 01:44:56.213
I love you.


01:44:58.006 --> 01:44:59.633
More than any other.


01:45:01.510 --> 01:45:03.011
And I would do anything for you.


01:45:04.763 --> 01:45:06.473
Everything I have is yours.


01:45:07.933 --> 01:45:09.935
How can you speak to me this way?


01:45:10.143 --> 01:45:12.729
Marguerite,
what way then would I speak to you?


01:45:14.648 --> 01:45:17.526
Milady must know it cannot be helped.


01:45:17.776 --> 01:45:21.113
My love for you has consumed me.


01:45:21.780 --> 01:45:22.739
How dare you?


01:45:22.948 --> 01:45:24.533
Milady, when milord
sets his course for love...


01:45:24.700 --> 01:45:25.868
You must leave now. Please.


01:45:26.034 --> 01:45:27.494
You heard the lady! Leave us.


01:45:27.661 --> 01:45:28.662
Milord.


01:45:39.298 --> 01:45:41.466
-I am married.
-Yes.


01:45:42.968 --> 01:45:44.803
And you are saddled
with a terrible burden.


01:45:46.555 --> 01:45:50.058
A cold, callous man
who does not love you as I do.


01:45:50.225 --> 01:45:52.227
Who cannot appreciate you
for the marvel that you are.


01:45:52.394 --> 01:45:54.646
Oh, please, do not speak of my husband.


01:45:54.813 --> 01:45:56.356
I want only for your happiness.


01:45:57.983 --> 01:46:01.236
I cannot bear to see you in such hardship.


01:46:02.362 --> 01:46:05.073
I know your house's finances are fragile.


01:46:05.282 --> 01:46:06.867
My lord provides for me.


01:46:07.075 --> 01:46:08.202
Yes.


01:46:13.665 --> 01:46:16.877
But does he know you
to be the most exquisite...


01:46:17.085 --> 01:46:18.462
fascinating woman?


01:46:20.255 --> 01:46:22.841
A woman I would devote my whole life to.


01:46:28.430 --> 01:46:30.682
Hear me say I'm in love with you.


01:46:33.393 --> 01:46:35.020
And I know...


01:46:35.187 --> 01:46:36.480
you love me too. You must.


01:46:37.439 --> 01:46:40.025
You must leave. Please.


01:46:46.532 --> 01:46:47.866
Marguerite, do not fight this.


01:47:13.225 --> 01:47:14.393
Jeanette!


01:47:19.481 --> 01:47:20.941
Jeanette!


01:47:24.152 --> 01:47:26.405
If you run, I will only chase you.


01:47:32.327 --> 01:47:33.787
Jeanette!


01:47:39.710 --> 01:47:42.462
No! No!


01:47:49.970 --> 01:47:51.138
Come here.


01:47:54.308 --> 01:47:55.392
No.


01:47:58.020 --> 01:47:59.897
No!


01:48:18.498 --> 01:48:21.585
No! No! No!


01:48:47.819 --> 01:48:48.737
No!


01:48:48.904 --> 01:48:50.656
No! Please.


01:48:50.864 --> 01:48:53.825
Please, don't do this.


01:48:55.452 --> 01:48:56.370
Please.


01:48:58.956 --> 01:49:00.374
This is our moment.


01:49:47.921 --> 01:49:49.339
Please.


01:50:20.871 --> 01:50:23.916
Oh, you feel yourself guilty.


01:50:24.166 --> 01:50:27.920
Oh, but, my love,
I beseech you, tell no one.


01:50:28.170 --> 01:50:30.339
For your own safety.


01:50:31.465 --> 01:50:33.967
If your husband hears of this,
he may kill you.


01:50:34.218 --> 01:50:35.260
Say nothing.


01:50:55.155 --> 01:50:57.241
Do not feel badly, my love.


01:50:59.201 --> 01:51:01.036
We could not help ourselves.


01:51:53.297 --> 01:51:55.549
Milady, we've returned.


01:52:06.643 --> 01:52:09.188
She was trying a new cook,
and the dish was quite tasty...


01:52:09.396 --> 01:52:10.814
save for the cheese.


01:52:10.981 --> 01:52:14.568
I've never enjoyed this particular cheese,
but sadly, it's everywhere.


01:52:15.944 --> 01:52:17.112
Thank you.


01:52:17.321 --> 01:52:19.656
There is one example...


01:52:19.865 --> 01:52:21.617
and I've forgotten the name of it...


01:52:23.410 --> 01:52:26.622
it has various colors laced through it.


01:52:28.916 --> 01:52:31.084
Do you know the name of this cheese?


01:52:31.293 --> 01:52:33.629
I think that it is Roquefort.


01:52:33.837 --> 01:52:37.549
No. No, no, not Roquefort.
It's not as strong as Roquefort.


01:52:37.716 --> 01:52:41.428
But it has a certain texture
that is very good in cookery.


01:52:46.683 --> 01:52:48.644
Milady.


01:52:48.810 --> 01:52:51.605
You haven't been eating.


01:52:51.813 --> 01:52:53.440
Are you ill?


01:52:56.360 --> 01:52:59.780
Lady Carrouges has enquired
about your state of mind.


01:53:02.199 --> 01:53:05.202
My state of mind is fine.
Thank you, Alice.


01:53:11.959 --> 01:53:13.669
Do not open the door.


01:53:14.503 --> 01:53:17.089
It's Marie. I'm here to see Marguerite.
Is she in?


01:53:20.175 --> 01:53:21.051
Fine.


01:53:23.846 --> 01:53:25.013
It's me.


01:53:28.600 --> 01:53:30.519
-Come on in.
-Good day.


01:53:34.064 --> 01:53:35.107
Marguerite!


01:53:37.067 --> 01:53:39.820
I've never felt such joy. I'm pregnant.


01:53:40.153 --> 01:53:42.489
I'm pregnant.


01:53:47.536 --> 01:53:49.204
Are you all right?


01:53:49.413 --> 01:53:50.998
You don't seem yourself.


01:53:53.250 --> 01:53:55.169
Are you not happy for me?


01:53:55.502 --> 01:53:56.920
I'm so very pleased for you.


01:54:08.849 --> 01:54:09.641
Sire.


01:54:16.857 --> 01:54:17.900
I have missed you.


01:54:21.069 --> 01:54:22.905
Did you not miss me?


01:54:23.864 --> 01:54:26.325
Oh, I missed you more than you know.


01:54:28.410 --> 01:54:30.829
-Then let us go to bed.
-Jean...


01:54:31.121 --> 01:54:33.707
-Marguerite, I've been away for many days.
-I cannot.


01:54:34.917 --> 01:54:36.919
What do you mean, you cannot?


01:54:40.672 --> 01:54:42.883
Well, I need to tell you something.


01:54:43.133 --> 01:54:44.218
What?


01:54:52.809 --> 01:54:53.727
What?


01:54:55.437 --> 01:54:58.941
While you were gone, there was a day
when your mother had business...


01:54:59.107 --> 01:55:00.317
in Saint Pierre.


01:55:00.526 --> 01:55:01.652
Yes.


01:55:03.028 --> 01:55:06.365
And shortly after,
a man came, unannounced.


01:55:08.492 --> 01:55:10.744
I knew the man, so I let him in.


01:55:13.956 --> 01:55:15.749
But he was not alone.


01:55:22.172 --> 01:55:25.300
Jacques Le Gris entered our home
without my permission and...


01:55:25.467 --> 01:55:27.970
-What about Le Gris?
-He forced me to this room.


01:55:29.054 --> 01:55:30.055
To this bed.


01:55:36.478 --> 01:55:37.604
He raped me.


01:55:39.690 --> 01:55:41.650
Are you telling me the truth?


01:55:42.192 --> 01:55:43.443
Please.


01:55:44.528 --> 01:55:46.446
Are you telling me the truth?


01:55:46.655 --> 01:55:50.158
Jean, please! I am telling you the truth.
You must believe me.


01:55:50.659 --> 01:55:51.994
I screamed.


01:55:52.202 --> 01:55:53.620
I screamed until I lost my voice.


01:55:53.787 --> 01:55:54.663
He forced you?


01:55:55.831 --> 01:55:56.790
He raped me.


01:55:56.957 --> 01:55:58.792
-You did not provoke this?
-No, Jean.


01:55:59.001 --> 01:56:00.085
Could you not run?


01:56:00.252 --> 01:56:02.963
I was pinned down, I could not breathe.


01:56:11.388 --> 01:56:15.392
Can this man do nothing but evil to me?


01:56:20.564 --> 01:56:22.900
Jean, I intend to speak the truth.


01:56:23.066 --> 01:56:25.903
I will not be silent.


01:56:31.742 --> 01:56:34.369
I have no legal standing
without your support.


01:56:44.796 --> 01:56:46.548
Then you shall have it.


01:56:50.219 --> 01:56:51.470
Come.


01:56:54.348 --> 01:56:56.767
I will not allow him to be the last man
to have known you.


01:56:58.143 --> 01:56:59.520
-Jean...
-Come.


01:57:05.108 --> 01:57:06.693
Come!


01:57:10.405 --> 01:57:12.616
Milady...


01:57:12.824 --> 01:57:15.077
do you swear upon your life...


01:57:15.285 --> 01:57:17.663
that what you say is true?


01:57:19.206 --> 01:57:20.541
I swear it.


01:57:21.250 --> 01:57:23.544
Will you swear it before God?


01:57:24.086 --> 01:57:25.754
And all of France?


01:57:28.841 --> 01:57:30.717
I will.


01:57:31.218 --> 01:57:32.344
Then we fight.


01:57:33.804 --> 01:57:35.013
Marguerite is my wife...


01:57:36.181 --> 01:57:39.184
and we have been wronged.


01:57:39.351 --> 01:57:41.353
I will not allow it to go unpunished.


01:57:41.562 --> 01:57:44.231
Your only avenue is through Pierre.


01:57:44.398 --> 01:57:45.983
Though I doubt he will give you a hearing.


01:57:46.191 --> 01:57:48.902
Tell the story you heard today.


01:57:49.069 --> 01:57:51.905
Tell it anywhere you can
and to all who will listen.


01:57:52.114 --> 01:57:54.241
We will be the subject of gossip.


01:57:54.408 --> 01:57:57.327
If the story is known across Normandy...


01:57:57.536 --> 01:58:00.038
Pierre will have to grant us a hearing.


01:58:01.665 --> 01:58:03.208
We have a plan.


01:58:15.304 --> 01:58:16.305
Marie?


01:58:19.266 --> 01:58:20.684
Stay a while.


01:58:22.895 --> 01:58:24.646
Why can't you look at me?


01:58:26.148 --> 01:58:27.357
I cannot.


01:58:27.566 --> 01:58:28.692
Marie?


01:58:29.735 --> 01:58:31.737
Do you not recall?


01:58:31.904 --> 01:58:34.781
You said, on one or more occasions,
that you found Le Gris handsome.


01:58:37.201 --> 01:58:38.202
So did you.


01:58:39.244 --> 01:58:40.537
But I do not complain of rape.


01:58:40.746 --> 01:58:42.080
Marie!


01:58:44.917 --> 01:58:46.084
You do not believe me.


01:58:49.171 --> 01:58:51.548
I have to go.


01:58:54.218 --> 01:58:58.055
No, Jean, no! This is not what I want!


01:58:58.263 --> 01:59:00.015
Not what you want?


01:59:00.807 --> 01:59:04.353
Can he not simply be tried for his crime
in the courts?


01:59:04.561 --> 01:59:07.272
Pierre is the courts!


01:59:07.523 --> 01:59:11.527
If you appeal to the king, he will only
side with Pierre as he has in the past.


01:59:14.947 --> 01:59:18.033
I will not appeal to the king.


01:59:18.325 --> 01:59:21.119
I will appeal to God.


01:59:29.211 --> 01:59:31.630
Marguerite, why have you done this?


01:59:32.214 --> 01:59:34.925
Because what happened to me is wrong.


01:59:35.175 --> 01:59:38.220
Men like Le Gris
take women when they want...


01:59:38.387 --> 01:59:40.180
and how often they want.


01:59:41.598 --> 01:59:43.267
Who do you think you are?


01:59:45.102 --> 01:59:46.728
My son may die.


01:59:48.063 --> 01:59:50.524
That is his choice. Not mine.


01:59:50.899 --> 01:59:53.902
You are no different from the peasants
our soldiers have their way with...


01:59:54.111 --> 01:59:56.238
when they are at war.


01:59:56.405 --> 01:59:57.614
Do they complain?


01:59:58.490 --> 02:00:00.701
I cannot be silent. I must speak.


02:00:00.951 --> 02:00:02.828
Marguerite!


02:00:02.995 --> 02:00:06.331
All you have done
is bring shame to our family.


02:00:08.625 --> 02:00:09.835
I am telling the truth.


02:00:10.043 --> 02:00:12.671
The truth does not matter.


02:00:16.425 --> 02:00:19.303
You look at me as if I were never young.


02:00:21.972 --> 02:00:23.974
I was raped.


02:00:26.894 --> 02:00:30.314
And despite my protestations
and my revulsion...


02:00:30.522 --> 02:00:33.108
did I go crying to my lord...


02:00:33.317 --> 02:00:34.610
who had better things to worry about?


02:00:34.818 --> 02:00:38.572
No, I stood up...


02:00:38.780 --> 02:00:40.365
got on with my life.


02:00:40.532 --> 02:00:42.075
But at what cost?


02:00:42.284 --> 02:00:43.619
At what cost?


02:00:47.164 --> 02:00:48.582
I'm alive.


02:00:50.000 --> 02:00:52.586
Well, you have paid a dear price
for that privilege.


02:00:55.923 --> 02:00:59.760
I have heard from several sources
that you told others...


02:01:00.010 --> 02:01:03.013
you found Monsieur Le Gris handsome.


02:01:04.890 --> 02:01:10.270
Perhaps you dreamt this event...


02:01:10.437 --> 02:01:12.189
wishing it to be true.


02:01:13.899 --> 02:01:17.819
Yes, a long time ago, some friends
and I agreed...


02:01:17.986 --> 02:01:21.406
that he was handsome, but I told them
that I knew him to be untrustworthy.


02:01:24.535 --> 02:01:28.330
Noticing a man is attractive
reveals nothing but that.


02:01:34.503 --> 02:01:36.672
And if one of these women
is your dearest friend...


02:01:36.964 --> 02:01:40.384
why would she bring this information
to the court?


02:01:41.885 --> 02:01:43.387
I do not know.


02:01:45.889 --> 02:01:50.269
You've been with Jean de Carrouges
for how many years?


02:01:50.435 --> 02:01:51.270
Five.


02:01:51.436 --> 02:01:53.355
In that time...


02:01:53.564 --> 02:01:55.649
you've not carried a child...


02:01:55.941 --> 02:01:57.484
an heir to the family name.


02:01:57.651 --> 02:02:00.112
No, monsieur. No.


02:02:01.613 --> 02:02:03.323
And yet, here you are...


02:02:03.532 --> 02:02:08.161
six months from the incident
you claim is true...


02:02:08.412 --> 02:02:10.831
and you are six months pregnant.


02:02:12.666 --> 02:02:14.501
Perhaps you have another lover...


02:02:14.710 --> 02:02:18.380
and accuse Le Gris to hide this.


02:02:18.797 --> 02:02:21.675
As I have said, I am loyal to my husband.


02:02:23.218 --> 02:02:26.138
Do you enjoy having intercourse
with your husband?


02:02:32.477 --> 02:02:34.271
Yes, of course.


02:02:34.563 --> 02:02:36.273
It is not a matter of course.


02:02:36.732 --> 02:02:39.151
You are fully aware
that you cannot conceive a child...


02:02:39.359 --> 02:02:41.278
unless you experience pleasure at the end.


02:02:41.361 --> 02:02:42.863
Yes.


02:02:43.030 --> 02:02:44.865
Yes.


02:02:45.032 --> 02:02:49.286
And do you experience pleasure at the end?


02:02:55.667 --> 02:02:57.920
Yes. I do.


02:02:58.170 --> 02:03:00.756
A rape cannot cause a pregnancy.


02:03:00.964 --> 02:03:02.090
This is just science.


02:03:02.883 --> 02:03:05.344
It permits the court to wonder...


02:03:05.511 --> 02:03:09.640
if after five years
of marital relations...


02:03:09.848 --> 02:03:12.267
your pregnancy is...


02:03:12.476 --> 02:03:14.394
a coincidence.


02:03:15.437 --> 02:03:19.816
Let us say we believe
you are telling the truth...


02:03:19.983 --> 02:03:24.238
and such an act
did, in fact, take place...


02:03:25.405 --> 02:03:27.616
perhaps you enjoyed it...


02:03:27.783 --> 02:03:30.827
more than you're willing to admit.


02:03:30.994 --> 02:03:34.289
Please, explain to me
how one is to enjoy rape.


02:03:34.498 --> 02:03:38.085
Did you experience pleasure?


02:03:41.255 --> 02:03:42.422
Simply answer the question.


02:03:42.589 --> 02:03:44.842
I experienced no pleasure!


02:03:50.013 --> 02:03:53.100
Are there any more questions?


02:03:58.438 --> 02:04:03.235
If your husband were to lose the duel,
it would demonstrate God's judgment...


02:04:04.319 --> 02:04:06.780
and reveal you
for having borne false witness.


02:04:07.489 --> 02:04:08.949
I understand.


02:04:09.199 --> 02:04:10.951
I'm certain your husband told you...


02:04:11.660 --> 02:04:16.206
the penalty for bearing false witness
against a man by a woman...


02:04:16.373 --> 02:04:18.542
in the case of rape...


02:04:18.750 --> 02:04:22.045
is that you are to be
stripped and shorn...


02:04:23.672 --> 02:04:27.259
fitted by the neck with an iron collar...


02:04:27.509 --> 02:04:31.138
lashed to a wooden post...


02:04:31.388 --> 02:04:33.265
and summarily burned alive.


02:04:37.311 --> 02:04:39.229
Lady Marguerite...


02:04:41.148 --> 02:04:43.525
it is quite common...


02:04:43.775 --> 02:04:47.905
for the accused to burn
for 20 to 30 minutes...


02:04:48.071 --> 02:04:49.907
before they are dead.


02:05:11.678 --> 02:05:13.138
I am telling the truth.


02:05:20.270 --> 02:05:21.855
We will proceed with the duel.


02:05:40.999 --> 02:05:43.377
You think Le Gris handsome, do you?


02:05:44.670 --> 02:05:46.171
You have disgraced me...


02:05:46.380 --> 02:05:48.590
before my king and all of France.


02:05:48.841 --> 02:05:52.177
You knew what would happen to me
should you lose this duel.


02:05:52.469 --> 02:05:53.679
You knew and you didn't tell me.


02:05:53.929 --> 02:05:55.973
God will not punish
those who tell the truth.


02:05:57.558 --> 02:06:02.771
My fate and our child's fate
will be written, not by God's will...


02:06:02.938 --> 02:06:05.440
but by which old man will tire first.


02:06:10.070 --> 02:06:11.613
How dare you speak to me this way.


02:06:11.864 --> 02:06:13.031
What have I to lose?


02:06:13.240 --> 02:06:16.159
I begged you to find another way,
and now I may be burned alive.


02:06:16.410 --> 02:06:18.537
I am risking my life for you.


02:06:20.747 --> 02:06:23.792
You are risking my life...


02:06:24.042 --> 02:06:26.545
so you can fight your enemy
and save your pride.


02:06:27.713 --> 02:06:30.215
And that could render our child an orphan.


02:06:32.634 --> 02:06:33.927
Or did you not think of that?


02:06:34.511 --> 02:06:36.180
You are a hypocrite.


02:06:37.389 --> 02:06:39.266
You are blinded by your vanity.


02:06:57.534 --> 02:06:58.994
All the preparations are made.


02:07:00.245 --> 02:07:02.122
I'm ready.


02:07:04.291 --> 02:07:06.919
I should like to stay a while longer.


02:07:09.588 --> 02:07:11.673
Faith, Marguerite.


02:07:11.882 --> 02:07:15.302
I finally gave birth to a son who I love
more than I could have ever imagined...


02:07:17.804 --> 02:07:20.390
and I may not live to see him grow.


02:07:24.978 --> 02:07:26.146
This was my life.


02:07:28.857 --> 02:07:31.693
Had I had known
the truth would deprive me of this love...


02:07:33.529 --> 02:07:37.074
I believe I would have done
what many women before me had done.


02:07:39.868 --> 02:07:41.828
Nothing.


02:07:42.788 --> 02:07:43.997
What you did was right.


02:07:45.415 --> 02:07:47.042
Not if I die.


02:07:50.504 --> 02:07:52.130
I am not like you, Jean.


02:07:55.968 --> 02:07:58.011
A child needs his mother...


02:07:58.178 --> 02:08:00.472
more than a mother needs to be right.


02:08:24.746 --> 02:08:26.665
Knights, proceed.


02:09:00.449 --> 02:09:01.241
Lady...


02:09:01.867 --> 02:09:03.493
upon your evidence...


02:09:03.660 --> 02:09:07.623
I hazard my life in combat
with Jacques Le Gris.


02:09:07.789 --> 02:09:10.918
You know my cause is just and true.


02:09:19.009 --> 02:09:21.428
I say before all of you...


02:09:21.929 --> 02:09:24.723
I spoke the truth.


02:09:25.349 --> 02:09:26.642
Let it be in God's hands.


02:09:56.088 --> 02:09:59.174
There'll be rough justice this day
by the grace of God.


02:10:03.387 --> 02:10:06.515
Let us pray this ends
like the duel at Flanders.


02:10:06.682 --> 02:10:11.645
With Le Gris in a wrestling match,
removing Carrouges' testicles by hand.


02:10:14.022 --> 02:10:15.607
Let them go!


02:10:15.941 --> 02:10:19.444
Let them go! Let them go!


02:10:31.790 --> 02:10:33.417
Quickly! Give it to me!


02:10:33.584 --> 02:10:36.295
Lance, lance! Hurry!


02:10:38.380 --> 02:10:39.381
Out of the way!


02:10:58.734 --> 02:11:00.652
Lance! Lance!


02:11:30.349 --> 02:11:31.183
Axe, axe!


02:14:53.093 --> 02:14:54.553
Carrouges may yet bleed out.


02:14:54.720 --> 02:14:55.846
Pray God.


02:15:02.311 --> 02:15:04.229
Kill him! Kill him!


02:15:10.485 --> 02:15:13.113
-Kill him!
-Kill him! Kill him!


02:16:09.127 --> 02:16:10.712
Confess!


02:16:15.717 --> 02:16:17.469
Confess to me.


02:16:19.471 --> 02:16:20.973
Carrouges, there was no rape.


02:16:24.810 --> 02:16:27.020
There was no rape.


02:16:30.232 --> 02:16:32.484
There was no rape!


02:16:37.239 --> 02:16:39.074
In the name of God...


02:16:39.241 --> 02:16:42.326
and on the peril of
damnation of my soul...


02:16:42.619 --> 02:16:44.620
I am innocent of the crime!


02:16:49.251 --> 02:16:52.921
Then you be damned.


02:17:09.730 --> 02:17:11.815
Yes.


02:18:03.700 --> 02:18:06.119
God be with you, milady.


02:18:14.253 --> 02:18:16.713
No... Rise. You rise.


02:18:18.549 --> 02:18:21.968
I grace you with honor, knight.


02:18:22.261 --> 02:18:24.221
God has spoken...


02:18:24.471 --> 02:18:28.642
proving your cause to be
truthful and just.


02:18:29.183 --> 02:18:33.063
You have fought
with strength and humility.


02:18:33.313 --> 02:18:37.066
May God be with you and your wife.


02:18:39.861 --> 02:18:40.946
Your wife.


02:20:15.123 --> 02:20:17.125
Long live Carrouges!


02:20:20.921 --> 02:20:22.130
Carrouges!


02:20:25.884 --> 02:20:27.761
The glory of Carrouges!


02:20:32.391 --> 02:20:33.684
Carrouges!


02:23:09.840 --> 02:23:11.300
Look at that!

